COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[49,"§As-Sahabul Khuboor\n‘As-Sahabul Khuboor’ means the buried bodies of the graves. The ‘Ahle Kitab’ or ’people of the book’ have been compared to the disbelievers in many places in the Holy Quran. But in the last verse of Surah Mumtahina, reference is made to an important aspect of Islam, namely belief in the Hereafter. The ‘people of the book’ claim to believe in the Hereafter but their actions speak differently. They act like the disbelievers who do not believe that they shall be resurrected.\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَوَلَّوْا قَوْمًا غَضِبَ اللَّـهُ عَلَيْهِمْ قَدْ يَئِسُوا مِنَ الْآخِرَةِ كَمَا يَئِسَ الْكُفَّارُ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ الْقُبُورِ ١٣﴾\nO you who have believed, do not make allies of a people with whom Allah has become angry. They have despaired of [reward in] the Hereafter just as the disbelievers have despaired of [meeting] the inhabitants of the graves.\n[Al-Mumtahina: 13]\nFor more details about grave, please look under the head ‘grave’."],[50,"§As-Sahabul Sabt\nAs-Sahabul Sabt means ‘people of Sabbath’. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ آمِنُوا بِمَا نَزَّلْنَا مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا مَعَكُم مِّن قَبْلِ أَن نَّطْمِسَ وُجُوهًا فَنَرُدَّهَا عَلَىٰ أَدْبَارِهَا أَوْ نَلْعَنَهُمْ كَمَا لَعَنَّا أَصْحَابَ السَّبْتِ ۚ وَكَانَ أَمْرُ اللَّـهِ مَفْعُولًا ٤٧﴾\nO you who were given the Scripture, believe in what We have sent down [to Muhammad], confirming that which is with you, before We obliterate faces and turn them toward their backs or curse them as We cursed the sabbath-breakers. And ever is the decree of Allah accomplished.\n[An-Nisa: 47]\n‘Sabt’ is a Jewish word which means ‘rest’. ‘Sabt’ is Saturday in English which is the last day of the week. According to the Jews, after creating this universe, God rested on this day.\nIn the book Genesis of the Holy Bible it says:\nThus the heavens and the earth were completed in all their vast array.\nBy the seventh day God had finished the work he had been doing; so on the seventh day he rested from all his work. Then God blessed the seventh day and made it holy, because on it he rested from all the work of creating that he had done.\n(Genesis 2:1-3)\nSimilarly in the book Exodus, it says:\n“Remember the Sabbath day by keeping it holy. Six days you shall labor and do all your work, but the seventh day is a sabbath to the LORD your God. On it you shall not do any work, neither you, nor your son or daughter, nor your male or female servant, nor your animals, nor any foreigner residing in your towns. For in six days the LORD made the heavens and the earth, the sea, and all that is in them, but he rested on the seventh day. Therefore the LORD blessed the Sabbath day and made it holy.\n(Exodus, 20:8-11)\nSevere punishment has been prescribed for those who violated the rule of the Sabbath. A man who was gathering wood on the Sabbath day was stoned to death. It says in the book Numbers of the Holy Bible:\nWhile the Israelites were in the wilderness, a man was found gathering wood on the Sabbath day. Those who found him gathering wood brought him to Moses and Aaron and the whole assembly, and they kept him in custody, because it was not clear what should be done to him. Then the LORD said to Moses, “The man must die. The whole assembly must stone him outside the camp.” So the assembly took him outside the camp and stoned him to death, as the LORD commanded Moses.\n(Numbers,15:32-36)\nIn the same way, the prophet Jeremiah(as), who belonged to the period 628-586 B.C. also threatened the Jews that if they worked on the Sabbath day, then he would burn down Jerusalem.\nBut if you do not obey me to keep the Sabbath day holy by not carrying any load as you come through the gates of Jerusalem on the Sabbath day, then I will kindle an unquenchable fire in the gates of Jerusalem that will consume her fortresses.’”\n(Jeremiah,17:27)\nSimilarly, prophet Ezekiel(as), who belonged to the period 595-536 B.C. warned the Jews against desecrating the Sabbath day.\nBut the Jews did not heed the warnings of their prophets concerning the Sabbath day and making various excuses, they continued working on the Sabbath. That is why Allah(swt) made them into despicable apes. Briefly in Surah-2, Al-Baqra and in detail in Surah-7, Al-Aaraf, Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ عَلِمْتُمُ الَّذِينَ اعْتَدَوْا مِنكُمْ فِي السَّبْتِ فَقُلْنَا لَهُمْ كُونُوا قِرَدَةً خَاسِئِينَ ٦٥﴾\nAnd you had already known about those who transgressed among you concerning the sabbath, and We said to them, \"Be apes, despised.\"\n[Al-Baqra: 65]\n﴿وَاسْأَلْهُمْ عَنِ الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِي كَانَتْ حَاضِرَةَ الْبَحْرِ إِذْ يَعْدُونَ فِي السَّبْتِ إِذْ تَأْتِيهِمْ حِيتَانُهُمْ يَوْمَ سَبْتِهِمْ شُرَّعًا وَيَوْمَ لَا يَسْبِتُونَ ۙ لَا تَأْتِيهِمْ ۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَبْلُوهُم بِمَا كَانُوا يَفْسُقُونَ ١٦٣﴾\nAnd ask them about the town that was by the sea - when they transgressed in [the matter of] the sabbath - when their fish came to them openly on their sabbath day, and the day they had no sabbath they did not come to them. Thus did We give them trial because they were defiantly disobedient.\n[Al-A’raf: 163]\nNeither the Holy Quran nor the Sahih Hadith mention the name of this city. But we can deduce from the way it is described that the Jews of Madina were aware of the city referred to because nobody raised any question regarding it. Scholars feel that this city is situated on the shores of the Qulzum (Clysma) sea. The incident about the people of that city turning into apes is not mentioned in the Holy Bible; from which we can say that this event took place after the revelation of the Holy Bible. But the Jews were aware of this.\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَجَعَلْنَاهَا نَكَالًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهَا وَمَا خَلْفَهَا وَمَوْعِظَةً لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ ٦٦﴾\nAnd We made it a deterrent punishment for those who were present and those who succeeded [them] and a lesson for those who fear Allah. [Al-Baqara: 66]\nThis proves that the Jews were well aware of the incident because only then would it serve as a warning to them. It is also clear that their physical appearance also became ape-like. If only their hearts had changed, it wouldn’t be enough as a deterrent and a lesson for them.\nIt is necessary to refute that the present day apes are not from the tribe of Bani-Israel who were turned into apes. According to Sahih Hadith:\nAllah(swt) does not continue the tribe of such people who due to some reason change their appearance (to resemble some other creature).\n(Sahih Muslim,2662)"],[51,"§As-Sahabul Safina\nAs-Sahabul Safina means ‘the people of the boat’. They are described in the Holy Quran as:\n﴿فَأَنجَيْنَاهُ وَأَصْحَابَ السَّفِينَةِ وَجَعَلْنَاهَا آيَةً لِّلْعَالَمِينَ ١٥﴾\nBut We saved him and the companions of the ship, and We made it a sign for the worlds.\n[Al-Ankaboot: 15]\nWho were these people in the boat? This is described in Surah Hud as follows:\n﴿حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَاءَ أَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّورُ قُلْنَا احْمِلْ فِيهَا مِن كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَأَهْلَكَ إِلَّا مَن سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ وَمَنْ آمَنَ ۚ وَمَا آمَنَ مَعَهُ إِلَّا قَلِيلٌ ٤٠﴾\n[So it was], until when Our command came and the oven overflowed, We said, \"Load upon the ship of each [creature] two mates and your family, except those about whom the word has preceded, and [include] whoever has believed.\" But none had believed with him, except a few.\n[Hud: 40]\nHere, what is meant by all types of creatures means all the animals which would be useful to him, because Nuh(as) wasn’t sent as a prophet to the whole world and moreover it is impossible to load on the ship a pair of every type of creature. It is equally wrong to suppose that the great flood drowned the whole earth.When he wasn’t sent as a messenger to the whole humanity, why would everybody who disbelieved in him be drowned?\nThe Holy Quran has rectified what has been distorted in the Holy Bible that the great flood submerged all the mountains, destroyed all the humans, animals, insects etc. and only those people remained who believed in Nuh(as) (Refer: Genesis 7:20-24). The Holy Quran does not say that the storm destroyed all the human beings. But some scholars say that the humans of these days are the descendants of Nuh(as). So, some other scholars say that when Nuh(as) was sent as a messenger, only his tribe existed on earth. Human civilization hadn’t spread to the other parts of the world. So, the great flood destroyed all the people except his believing family and the believers.\nIs there any description of the great flood in the ancient history of the places like India, Australia etc? All these people are from the offspring of Nuh(as) who slowly spread to these parts and have recorded ancient history for the future generations because other than Gazala and Furat of Iraq, no other place has any signs of the great flood. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَقِيلَ يَا أَرْضُ ابْلَعِي مَاءَكِ وَيَا سَمَاءُ أَقْلِعِي وَغِيضَ الْمَاءُ وَقُضِيَ الْأَمْرُ وَاسْتَوَتْ عَلَى الْجُودِيِّ ۖ وَقِيلَ بُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ ٤٤﴾\nAnd it was said, \"O earth, swallow your water, and O sky, withhold [your rain].\" And the water subsided, and the matter was accomplished, and the ship came to rest on the [mountain of] Judiyy. And it was said, \"Away with the wrongdoing people.\" [Hud: 44]\nWhere is this mountain Judiyy? The Holy Quran or the Sahih Hadith do not answer this question. The Holy Bible calls this the ‘Ararat’ mountain. (Genesis 8:4). Christian scholars are of the opinion that this mountain is in Armenia which is 16916 ft. above sea level. (Refer to Khamoos, Kitab Muqaddas, p.42)\nThe Muslim scholars agree with this view. They say that the mountain Judiyy is between the Arabic peninsula and Moosil which is a famous city of Iraq. Even today this mountain is called Judiyy. (Refer to: Tafheemul-Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-44, S.46)"],[52,"§As-Sahabul-Uqdood\nThis means ‘the people of the trench’. Their description is given in Surah Buruj which says:\n﴿قُتِلَ أَصْحَابُ الْأُخْدُودِ ٤ النَّارِ ذَاتِ الْوَقُودِ ٥ إِذْ هُمْ عَلَيْهَا قُعُودٌ ٦ وَهُمْ عَلَىٰ مَا يَفْعَلُونَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ شُهُودٌ ٧ وَمَا نَقَمُوا مِنْهُمْ إِلَّا أَن يُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّـهِ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَمِيدِ ٨ الَّذِي لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۚ وَاللَّـهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ ٩﴾\nCursed were the companions of the trench. [Containing] the fire full of fuel, When they were sitting near it. And they, to what they were doing against the believers, were witnesses. And they resented them not except because they believed in Allah, the Exalted in Might, the Praiseworthy, To whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. And Allah, over all things, is Witness.\n[Al-Buruj: 4-9]\nIn these verses a historical event is being referred to, whose description is given in the book ‘Kitab-e-Siyar’ written by Ibn-Ishaq as follows: The Himyari king of Yemen, Dhunawas who was a Jew, attacked the neighboring Nazranis who were the followers of Isa(as). He ordered them to either embrace Judaism or face death. When they refused to become Jews, he ordered a deep trench to be dug, filled it with a blazing fire and ordered that they be thrown into the flames. It is said that he killed twenty thousand people in this way. He not only murdered them but also sat near the trench and gleefully watched the people die. When the king of Rome came to know about it, he ordered the African king, who was a Christian to attack Yemen. Seventy thousand African soldiers attacked Yemen. The evil king was defeated and thus ended the Jewish rule. This event occurred around 523 A.D.\nThis description has one contradiction. The Jewish king Dhunawas attacked the neighboring Nazran because they had embraced Christianity and he wanted them to accept Judaism while there exists historical proof that the people of Nazran were idol-worshippers. In that case how could the king order them to accept Judaism when it was only meant exclusively for Bani-Israel? No other person could enter it and even if he did the Jews would not accept him. So, even if this incident is true, the reason for the attack could be that he did not want a Christian kingdom to be established in his neighborhood who along with the African kingdom could pose problems for the Jewish state. So, he may have wanted the people of Nazran to go back to idol-worship so that they would not become the allies of the African people.\nSo, the correct version is what is given in Sahih Muslim as narrated by the Holy Prophet(saws). The king of Nazran had a magician in his court. When he became old, he asked the king for an obedient boy to whom he could teach the magic. He was given such a boy. On the way to the magician’s place the boy would meet a padre everyday and one day he accepted the padre’s religion. Allah(swt) gave him the power to perform certain miracles like restoring sight to the blind and curing lepers. When the magician came to know that the boy had started believing in the ‘Unity of God’, he got the padre killed and then tried to get the boy killed in which he was unsuccessful. The boy then told the king that if he wanted to kill him, he should assemble the people and then shoot an arrow saying ‘In the name of the Lord of this boy’. The king did so and the boy was killed. Seeing this all the people shouted ‘We believe in the Lord of this boy’. Seeing this the king was furious and said ‘The very thing which we wanted to prevent has happened’. He ordered deep trenches to be dug and filled it with blazing fire and filled it with the people who refused to turn away from Christianity.(Refer to Sahih Muslim, 3005). Twenty thousand people were thrown into the fire in this way. According to the history of Nazran this version appears correct because the people of Nazran were polytheists and when they became believers, the disbeliever king tormented them this way.\n﴿إِذْ هُمْ عَلَيْهَا قُعُودٌ ٦ وَهُمْ عَلَىٰ مَا يَفْعَلُونَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ شُهُودٌ ٧ وَمَا نَقَمُوا مِنْهُمْ إِلَّا أَن يُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّـهِ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَمِيدِ ٨﴾\nWhen they were sitting near it. And they, to what they were doing against the believers, were witnesses. And they resented them not except because they believed in Allah, the Exalted in Might, the Praiseworthy,\n[Al-Burooj: 6-8]\nThe description of the event of As-Sahabul-Uqdood is also given in the writings and books of the scholars of the 6th century A.D. Three of these were contemporaries: Procopius, Kosmas and Johans Ifsosi. Similarly after them many other Christian writers have described this event in great detail.Some people have even located the place where the trenches were dug. The people of Nazran are aware of the place even today.\nBy describing ‘As-Sahabul-Uqdood’, the Holy Quran is exhorting the believers to have patience in the face of the various forms of torment which the disbelievers of Mecca were subjecting them to, as a day will surely come when Islam would spread to all four corners of the earth. As prophesied, all the plots of the disbelievers back-fired, the disbelievers were destroyed and Mecca became ‘Darul-Islam’."],[53,"§As-Sahabur Rass\nAs-Sahabur Rass means ‘people of the well’. ‘Rass’ is the Arabic word for well. As-Sahabur Rass are mentioned in two places in the Holy Quran but nowhere is a detailed description given. There is no explanation even in the Sahih Hadith. That is why there is a difference of opinion among the scholars regarding this. Imam Tabri has expressed his views as follows:\n‘Rass’ means a well. The people called ‘As-Sahabur Rass’ in the Holy Quran rejected the message of their prophets and threw them into a well. Hence they are called ‘As-Sahabur Rass’.\n‘Rass’ is the name of a valley near Aizerbaijan which was inhabited by thousands of tribes. They rejected the message of their prophets as a result of which Allah(swt) destroyed them. (Maybe Russia is indicated here)\n‘Rass’ could also mean ‘cave’ so this must mean ‘As-Sahabul Uqdood’.\nThis third supposition is wrong because ‘As-Sahabur Rass’ belonged to the period before Isa(as) whereas ‘As-Sahabul Uqdood’ belonged to the second or third century A.D. Whoever they were, the Holy Quran mentions them along with the tribes who rejected the true faith and the message of the messengers who were sent to them, as a result of which Allah(swt) destroyed them.\n﴿وَعَادًا وَثَمُودَ وَأَصْحَابَ الرَّسِّ وَقُرُونًا بَيْنَ ذَٰلِكَ كَثِيرًا ٣٨﴾\nAnd [We destroyed] 'Aad and Thamud and the companions of the well and many generations between them.\n[Al-Furqan: 38]\nThe fact that many generations existed between them proves that ‘As-Sahabur Rass’ belonged to the period before Isa(as).\n﴿كَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ وَأَصْحَابُ الرَّسِّ وَثَمُودُ ١٢ وَعَادٌ وَفِرْعَوْنُ وَإِخْوَانُ لُوطٍ ١٣ وَأَصْحَابُ الْأَيْكَةِ وَقَوْمُ تُبَّعٍ ۚ كُلٌّ كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ وَعِيدِ ١٤﴾\nThe people of Noah denied before them, and the companions of the well and Thamud. And 'Aad and Pharaoh and the brothers of Lot .And the companions of the thicket and the people of Tubba'. All denied the messengers, so My threat was justly fulfilled.\n[Qaf: 12-14]\nAn Egyptian scholar is of the opinion that ‘rass’ actually means ‘Urs’ which is a prominent city of ‘Qafqaz’. A messenger named ‘Zurdust’ had been sent to this place. He warned them about Allah(swt), but they did not heed him as a result of which Allah(swt) destroyed them. He then left for Iran and spread his message there. His famous book ‘Avesta’ or ‘Usta’ makes a prediction regarding Muhammad(saws). ‘Ibn-Kasir’ also discusses the opinions of some scholars who say that ‘Rass’ is a well near Aizerbaijan and that is the reason they were called ‘As-Sahabur-Rass’.\nWe cannot definitely say as to which tribe is meant and this is not the main aim of the Holy Quran. The purpose of the Holy Quran in describing these people is to warn others that just as these tribes were destroyed for rejecting the Holy Prophet Muhammad(saws), if they do not follow the one and only right path, even they shall suffer the same fate.\nAs predicted, the powerful chiefs and leaders were defeated, and in just a matter of ten years Muslims triumphed over Mecca and Islam entered each and every house."],[54,"§Atrocity(Wrong or injustice)\nIn the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith, atrocities(wrongs) have been severely criticized. The perpetrators of atrocities have been warned in the Holy Quran as:\n﴿إِلَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ وَذَكَرُوا اللَّـهَ كَثِيرًا وَانتَصَرُوا مِن بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوا ۗ وَسَيَعْلَمُ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا أَيَّ مُنقَلَبٍ يَنقَلِبُونَ ٢٢٧﴾\nExcept those [poets] who believe and do righteous deeds and remember Allah often and defend [the Muslims] after they were wronged. And those who have wronged are going to know to what [kind of] return they will be returned.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 227]\n﴿وَلَوْ أَنَّ لِلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا مَا فِي الْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا وَمِثْلَهُ مَعَهُ لَافْتَدَوْا بِهِ مِن سُوءِ الْعَذَابِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ ۚ وَبَدَا لَهُم مِّنَ اللَّـهِ مَا لَمْ يَكُونُوا يَحْتَسِبُونَ ٤٧﴾\nAnd if those who did wrong had all that is in the earth entirely and the like of it with it, they would [attempt to] ransom themselves thereby from the worst of the punishment on the Day of Resurrection. And there will appear to them from Allah that which they had not taken into account.\n[Az-Zumar: 47]\nAccording to Sahih Hadith:\n“The people who perpetrate atrocities in this world will be in pitch darkness on Doomsday, they shall see no ray of light to escape the punishment of Allah(swt).”\n(Bukhari, 2447; Muslim,2579)\nIn the Holy Quran, the word ‘wrong’ has also been used in another sense. That is, replacing a thing with another. For example:\nAllah(swt) is the Creator of this entire universe. He(swt) is its Sustainer. He(swt) is the One with all the best Qualities and the Most Powerful. So, He(swt) is the only One worthy of worship. Therefore, instead of worshipping the One true Lord, if somebody worships somebody else, then it is the greatest wrong in the sight of Allah(swt). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ لُقْمَانُ لِابْنِهِ وَهُوَ يَعِظُهُ يَا بُنَيَّ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِاللَّـهِ ۖ إِنَّ الشِّرْكَ لَظُلْمٌ عَظِيمٌ ١٣﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when Luqman said to his son while he was instructing him, \"O my son, do not associate [anything] with Allah. Indeed, association [with him] is great injustice.\"\n[Luqman: 13]\nIt is considered wrong to break rules. Breaking the existing rules, a man does wrong against himself. It is said in the Holy Quran that by going against the rules set by Allah(swt), a man harms himself because he cannot harm Allah(swt) in any way. [Al-Baqara: 231] [At-Talaq: 1]\nAllah(swt) never wrongs anybody but they wrong against themselves because whatever punishment they face is a result of their own wrongs. (see Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-101; Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-118; Surah-43, Az-Zukhruf, Verse-76)\nOn the Day of Judgement, no one will be wronged:\n﴿وَنَضَعُ الْمَوَازِينَ الْقِسْطَ لِيَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ فَلَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌ شَيْئًا ۖ وَإِن كَانَ مِثْقَالَ حَبَّةٍ مِّنْ خَرْدَلٍ أَتَيْنَا بِهَا ۗ وَكَفَىٰ بِنَا حَاسِبِينَ ٤٧﴾\nAnd We place the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection, so no soul will be treated unjustly at all. And if there is [even] the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it forth. And sufficient are We as accountant.\n[Al-Anbiya: 47]\nThe worst wrong-doers described in the Holy Quran are:\ni. Polytheists\nii. Those who stop people from praying in the mosques\n﴿وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّن مَّنَعَ مَسَاجِدَ اللَّـهِ أَن يُذْكَرَ فِيهَا اسْمُهُ وَسَعَىٰ فِي خَرَابِهَا ۚ أُولَـٰئِكَ مَا كَانَ لَهُمْ أَن يَدْخُلُوهَا إِلَّا خَائِفِينَ ۚ لَهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيَا خِزْيٌ وَلَهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ ١١٤﴾\n[Al-Baqara: 114]\niii. Those who hide the testimonies which have come from Allah(swt)\n﴿أَمْ تَقُولُونَ إِنَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْبَاطَ كَانُوا هُودًا أَوْ نَصَارَىٰ ۗ قُلْ أَأَنتُمْ أَعْلَمُ أَمِ اللَّـهُ ۗ وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّن كَتَمَ شَهَادَةً عِندَهُ مِنَ اللَّـهِ ۗ وَمَا اللَّـهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ ١٤٠﴾\n[Al-Baqara: 140]\niv. Those who invent lies about Allah(swt)\n﴿وَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرَىٰ عَلَى اللَّـهِ كَذِبًا أَوْ كَذَّبَ بِآيَاتِهِ ۗ إِنَّهُ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظَّالِمُونَ ٢١﴾\n[Al-An’am: 21]\nv. Those who deny or turn away from the verses of Allah(swt)\n﴿أَوْ تَقُولُوا لَوْ أَنَّا أُنزِلَ عَلَيْنَا الْكِتَابُ لَكُنَّا أَهْدَىٰ مِنْهُمْ ۚ فَقَدْ جَاءَكُم بَيِّنَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَهُدًى وَرَحْمَةٌ ۚ فَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّن كَذَّبَ بِآيَاتِ اللَّـهِ وَصَدَفَ عَنْهَا ۗ سَنَجْزِي الَّذِينَ يَصْدِفُونَ عَنْ آيَاتِنَا سُوءَ الْعَذَابِ بِمَا كَانُوا يَصْدِفُونَ ١٥٧﴾\n[Al-An’am: 157]\nIf the wrong-doers repent for their sins, Allah(swt) will forgive them if He(swt) Wills:\n﴿فَمَن تَابَ مِن بَعْدِ ظُلْمِهِ وَأَصْلَحَ فَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَتُوبُ عَلَيْهِ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ٣٩﴾\nand\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ إِذَا فَعَلُوا فَاحِشَةً أَوْ ظَلَمُوا أَنفُسَهُمْ ذَكَرُوا اللَّـهَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا لِذُنُوبِهِمْ وَمَن يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ إِلَّا اللَّـهُ وَلَمْ يُصِرُّوا عَلَىٰ مَا فَعَلُوا وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ ١٣٥﴾\nBut whoever repents after his wrongdoing and reforms, indeed, Allah will turn to him in forgiveness. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 39] [Al-i-Imran: 135]\nRepentance means that if a person has unjustly taken somebody’s wealth, he should return it. If somebody has hurt somebody, then he should seek the victim’s forgiveness and also beg Allah(swt)’s forgiveness saying that he will not harm anyone else in the future. Then Allah(swt) will have mercy on him and accept his repentance. This is called ‘Tawba an-Nasooh’."],[55,"§Ayyub(as)\nAyyub(as) was a prophet. Allah(swt) sent the revelation to him. At one place the Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِنَّا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ كَمَا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ نُوحٍ وَالنَّبِيِّينَ مِن بَعْدِهِ ۚ وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْبَاطِ وَعِيسَىٰ وَأَيُّوبَ وَيُونُسَ وَهَارُونَ وَسُلَيْمَانَ ۚ وَآتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ زَبُورًا ١٦٣﴾\nIndeed, We have revealed to you, [O Muhammad], as We revealed to Noah and the prophets after him. And we revealed to Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob, the Descendants, Jesus, Job, Jonah, Aaron, and Solomon, and to David We gave the book [of Psalms].\n[An-Nisa: 163]\nFrom the above verse, we come to know that Ayyub(as) was born after Ibraheem(as). Some scholars say that his father’s name was ‘Amoos’ and that he was from the family of Isu-bin-Ishaq-bin-Ibraheem. They say that his wife ‘Rehma’ was the grand-daughter of Hazrat Yusuf and the daughter of Ifraheem-bin-Yusuf. In the Jewish ‘Old Testament’, one whole book is dedicated to him which in turn has forty-two parts. We come to know from this that he was an inhabitant of ‘Awas’ which is near Damascus. Some are of the opinion that ‘Awas’ is the same city which is known as ‘Harraan’ and is situated to the north of Damascus. He was extremely wealthy and had seven sons and three daughters. Then it so happened that he lost all his wealth, all his children died and he was afflicted with a terrible disease due to which everybody left him. Only his wife remained with him. But all through his sufferings, he was extremely patient and just prayed to Allah(swt). Allah(swt) narrates this in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنَا أَيُّوبَ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ أَنِّي مَسَّنِيَ الشَّيْطَانُ بِنُصْبٍ وَعَذَابٍ ٤١﴾\nAnd remember Our servant Job, when he called to his Lord, \"Indeed, Satan has touched me with hardship and torment.\"\n[Sad: 41]\nIt is said here that Satan has caused him torment when according to Islamic teachings, Allah(swt) is the only One who can give either joys or troubles. Maybe Ayyub(as) has related his troubles to the Satan instead of Allah(swt) because he felt that the schemes and distractions of the Satan were the cause of his troubles. Or maybe he considered it as against Allah(swt)’s Majesty to think so. In another verse, it does not say that the troubles are from Satan :\n﴿وَأَيُّوبَ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ أَنِّي مَسَّنِيَ الضُّرُّ وَأَنتَ أَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِينَ ٨٣﴾\nAnd [mention] Job, when he called to his Lord, \"Indeed, adversity has touched me, and you are the Most Merciful of the merciful.\"\n[Al-Anbiya: 83]\nBy describing the courage and patience of Ayyub(as), Allah(swt) wants to tell the believers that troubles did afflict the earlier messengers and prophets, which they faced with lots of courage and patience. They never left their true faith but cheerfully endured everything and simply prayed to Allah(swt) to end their hardships. The same thing happened in Ayyub(as)’s case. He prayed to Allah(swt). Allah(swt) heard him and instructed him thus:\n﴿ارْكُضْ بِرِجْلِكَ ۖ هَـٰذَا مُغْتَسَلٌ بَارِدٌ وَشَرَابٌ ٤٢﴾\n[So he was told], \"Strike [the ground] with your foot; this is a [spring for] a cool bath and drink.\"\n[Sad: 42]\nThat is when you bathe in this water, you will be cured externally and when you drink it, you will be cured internally.\nAnd moreover:\n﴿وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُ أَهْلَهُ وَمِثْلَهُم مَّعَهُمْ رَحْمَةً مِّنَّا وَذِكْرَىٰ لِأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ ٤٣﴾\nAnd We granted him his family and a like [number] with them as mercy from Us and a reminder for those of understanding.\n[Sad: 43]\nThat is, his family was doubled compared to what he had before his family had perished. It is said that Allah(swt) made his wife young again and she gave birth to seven sons and three daughters.\n(See Bible, Job 42:13)\nTherefore not only was his family given back to him, but was also doubled. Before that only his wife was left with him who would single-handedly serve him. One day for some reason he was angry with her and had vowed that when he became healthy again he would give her a hundred lashes. Allah(swt) instructed Ayyub(as):\n﴿وَخُذْ بِيَدِكَ ضِغْثًا فَاضْرِب بِّهِ وَلَا تَحْنَثْ ۗ إِنَّا وَجَدْنَاهُ صَابِرًا ۚ نِّعْمَ الْعَبْدُ ۖ إِنَّهُ أَوَّابٌ ٤٤﴾\n[We said], \"And take in your hand a bunch [of grass] and strike with it and do not break your oath.\" Indeed, We found him patient, an excellent servant. Indeed, he was one repeatedly turning back [to Allah].\n[Sad: 44]\nIn this way Allah(swt) in His infinite wisdom not only made sure that Ayyub(as) kept his vow, but also saved his pious wife from painful punishment.\nFrom these verses, scholars have deduced many Islamic rules whose description is beyond the scope of this book.\nIn this way, Allah(swt) in His infinite mercy, ordered His slave Ayyub(as) to just hit his pious wife, who had selflessly served him in his affliction, with a bunch of grass of a hundred blades so that his vow was fulfilled.\nAccording to the story of Ayyub(as) as told in the Holy Quran, during his misfortune he was always turned towards Allah(swt), body and soul and would intensely pray to Allah(swt) to end his troubles. This is ‘Tawheed’ because those who believe in ‘Tawheed’ or ‘Oneness of God’ never seek favors from or believe in other god-goddesses, jinn, satan etc. as the polytheists of Mecca were doing. We learn from the life of Ayyub(as) that Allah(swt) alone can help us in times of distress and none other has any power to do the slightest harm or grant any benefit other than Him. This is ‘Tawheed’ towards which all the prophets invited the people of this world.\nHe lived to see three generations of his family and passed away at the ripe old age of 140. The well where Ayyub(as) bathed is still in existence today in a village called ‘Nawa’ in Syria which is popularly known as the ‘well of Ayyub(as)’ and his tomb is also present here. More information can be found in the Jewish ‘Old Testament’ book of Job. We also come to know from it that the Satan tried to mislead him in many ways but Ayyub(as) was steadfast in his faith. This book gives his brief life-history and is based on the questions and answers between his friends Temani Elipuz, Shuhi Bildad and Sopar and is in a poetic style.\nIn this book there is no mention of either Musa(as) or Bani-Israel. So, probably he must have been born after Ibraheem(as) and before Musa(as)."],[56,"§Azaab\nThe word ‘Azaab’ occurs again and again in the Holy Quran. It means the painful retribution from Allah(swt) which the disbelievers have to endure. It may be in this world itself which the powerful chieftains of Mecca faced in the battle of Badr or it may be in the Hereafter. Not believing in Allah(swt) and His last Messenger(saws) is the greatest of sins. It is rejecting the Sovereignty of the One and Only God who has given us our very life, created the sun and the moon, given us our livelihood and innumerable things to lead a happy and comfortable life. In return if we do not obey His commands, the remuneration for this ungratefulness is nothing but painful torment.\nThe Holy Quran is the only book on earth which gives a detailed description of the painful punishment of the Hereafter. The other religious books just make a mention of it. It is one of the miracles of the Holy Quran that it gives a complete explanation about the various aspects of faith so that no doubt is left in the hearts of the followers. This faith was propagated by all the prophets but their followers distorted the facts.\nThere will be two kinds of people who will face torment.\nTo the first kind belong the people and tribes who did not believe in Allah(swt), rejected His Prophet(saws) and his teachings and also disbelieved the other prophets. At numerous places in the Holy Quran, these tribes of the various prophets are mentioned and the wrath of Allah(swt) which they incurred as a result of their disbelief is described. They got their retribution in this world which was quite painful; but they will have to face an even greater torment in the Hereafter.\nTo the second category belong the people who are believers but caused either physical or mental injury to others or who trampled on others’ rights and did not seek their forgiveness. So, in return they will have to bear the punishment on the day of Judgement. Only after that shall they enter heaven.\nSome rules have been given in the Holy Quran with regard to the retribution:\n1.\n﴿مَّنِ اهْتَدَىٰ فَإِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِي لِنَفْسِهِ ۖ وَمَن ضَلَّ فَإِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَا ۚ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ ۗ وَمَا كُنَّا مُعَذِّبِينَ حَتَّىٰ نَبْعَثَ رَسُولًا ١٥﴾\nWhoever is guided is only guided for [the benefit of] his soul. And whoever errs only errs against it. And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another. And never would We punish until We sent a messenger.\n[Al-Isra: 15]\nOnly in the case of Prophet Muhammad(saws) it has been said:\n﴿وَمَا كَانَ اللَّـهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَأَنتَ فِيهِمْ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ اللَّـهُ مُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُونَ ٣٣﴾\nBut Allah would not punish them while you, [O Muhammad], are among them, and Allah would not punish them while they seek forgiveness.\n[Al-Anfal: 33]\nEven though the disbelievers from the tribe of Prophet Muhammad(saws) had said:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالُوا اللَّـهُمَّ إِن كَانَ هَـٰذَا هُوَ الْحَقَّ مِنْ عِندِكَ فَأَمْطِرْ عَلَيْنَا حِجَارَةً مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ أَوِ ائْتِنَا بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ ٣٢﴾\nAnd [remember] when they said, \"O Allah, if this should be the truth from You, then rain down upon us stones from the sky or bring us a painful punishment.\"\n[Al-Anfal: 32]\nBut because Prophet Muhammad(saws) had been sent as a mercy to the whole world, Allah(swt) saved his tribe from punishment even though Jibrail(as) had said that if the Prophet(saws) willed, he would crush the disbelievers between two mountains. The Holy Prophet(saws) forbade him saying that from among the progeny of these disbelievers, there would be some pious and righteous people who would help in propagating Islam. This prophecy did come true.\n2. Before the retribution, a final warning will be given and the pious will be brought out from the place.\n3. After the retribution comes, repentance will not be accepted.\n4. However harsh the retribution in this world, the punishment of the Hereafter will be worse. (Refer: Quran,Surah-2, Al-Baqra, Verse-85 and Surah-13, Ar-Ra’d,Verse-34)\n5. Besides the disbelievers and polytheists, the people who indulge in adultery, gambling, intoxication, blasphemy etc. which go against the teachings of Islam will also face retribution in this world. Calamities like earthquakes, cyclones, tempests etc. will wipe out these people from the face of the earth.\nThe above mentioned are a few rules of retribution."],[57,"§Azaan\n‘Azaan’ means ‘to call’ or ‘proclaim’. Allah(swt) orders Ibraheem(as) in the Holy Quran to call people for Haj:\n﴿وَأَذِّن فِي النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ يَأْتُوكَ رِجَالًا وَعَلَىٰ كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ يَأْتِينَ مِن كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيقٍ ٢٧﴾\nAnd proclaim to the people the Hajj [pilgrimage]; they will come to you on foot and on every lean camel; they will come from every distant pass\n[Al-Hajj: 27]\nIn the early stages of Islam, the Muslims did not have any specific means of announcing the time for Salah. Some suggested that they should ring a bell like the Christians to announce the time for prayer while some others said that they should blow the conch like the Jews. Hazrat Umar(ra) suggested that somebody should go around calling out ‘Namaz Namaz’. This method pleased the Holy Prophet(saws) and he asked Bilal to do it.(Bukhari 604, Muslim 377)\nBut the Holy Prophet(saws) continued to think about it when one day Abdullah-bin-Zaid-bin-Abd Rabhi approached him and said “O Prophet of Allah(swt), I was in a half-awakened state when a man came up to me and pronounced the azaan”. Umar(ra) then said, “Twenty days back even I saw the same thing”. Then, the Holy Prophet(saws) instructed Bilal to give the azaan because he had a sweet and loud voice. From that day onwards in all the mosques, azaan is given to announce the salah. In the azaan, first Allah(swt) is praised, then testimony is given that there is no God but Allah(swt), then the testimony about Muhammad(saws) being the messenger of Allah(swt) is given and then the call is given for the prayer. The following is the translation of the azaan :\nAllahu Akbar Allahu Akbar Allah(swt) is the Greatest. Allah(swt) is the Greatest. (twice)\nAshhadu an la ilaha illa Allah I bear witness that there is no god except Allah(swt). (twice)\nAshhadu anna Muhammadan Rasool Allah I bear witness that Muhammad(saws) is the messenger of Allah(swt).(twice)\nHayya 'ala-s-Salah Come to the prayer (twice)\nHayya 'ala-l-Falah Come to success (twice)\nAllahu Akbar Allahu Akbar Allah(swt) is the Greatest. Allah(swt) is the Greatest.\nLa ilaha illa Allah There is no god except Allah(swt).\nFor the pre-dawn (fajr) prayer, the following phrase is inserted after the fifth part above, towards the end:\nAs-salatu Khayrun Minan-nawm Prayer is better than sleep. (twice)\nIt is compulsory for every Muslim who hears the azaan to reply to it. He should softly repeat whatever is pronounced in the azaan. Except when Hayya 'ala-s-Salah and Hayya 'ala-l-Falah are pronounced the listener should reply with ‘La haula wa la Khuwwata illa Billah.’\nThat is, we have no strength to come to the salah and attain success except if Allah(swt) Wills. In a way man proclaims his insignificance compared to the Majesty of Allah(swt).\nThe real response on hearing the azaan is to forget whatever we are doing and hurry for salah; but the Holy Prophet(saws) has asked us to even repeat whatever is pronounced as described above.\nAfter the azaan, there is a specific dua(supplication) which has been given in the Sahih Hadith. On reciting it, the Holy Prophet(saws) will intercede for us on the Day of Judgement.\nAccording to Sahih Hadith, the head of the muezzin will be raised high on the Day of Judgement.(Muslim, 387)\nAccording to another Sahih Hadith, all those present within the muezzin’s earshot will bear witness for him.(Abu Dawood,515)."],[58,"§Azar\nAzar is the name of the father of Ibraheem(as). He is described only once in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ لِأَبِيهِ آزَرَ أَتَتَّخِذُ أَصْنَامًا آلِهَةً ۖ إِنِّي أَرَاكَ وَقَوْمَكَ فِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٧٤﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when Abraham said to his father Azar, \"Do you take idols as deities? Indeed, I see you and your people to be in manifest error.\"\n[Al-An’am: 74]\nIn the Taurah, the name of the father of Ibraheem(as) is mentioned as ‘Tare’. We can either suppose that the writer of Taurah committed a mistake or that ‘Azar’ is an attribute of Tare. Other than this whatever else is supposed is wrong.\nAzar was a trader in ‘Ur’. In those days the people of Iraq worshipped gods and goddesses with great pomp and show, especially the moon. They sculpted the gods and goddesses with their own hands and then worshipped them. They did not even understand that what they themselves had created could not grant them any favors or benefit them in any way. Azar had three sons – Haraan, Ibraheem and Nahaur. Lut(as) was the offspring of Haraan, who is described later on. Haraan died in Ur itself. Nahaur, the younger brother of Ibraheem had twelve sons and all of them stayed on in Ur. But Azar took Ibraheem(as) and Haraan’s son Lut to the city of Haraan in Syria and later on he died there.\nSo we can deduce that the argument which took place between prophet Ibraheem(as) and Azar was in Haraan because it says in the Taurah:\nThe LORD had said to Abram, “Go from your country, your people and your father’s household to the land I will show you.\n“I will make you into a great nation, and I will bless you; I will make your name great, and you will be a blessing (Bible: Genesis,12:1-2)\nIt is understood from the Taurah that at the age of 205, Azar died in Haraan itself but he hadn’t given up idol-worship. Ibraheem(as) hoped that he would stop idolatry and that he would pray to Allah(swt) for his father’s forgiveness. But, when he did not give up idol-worship, Ibraheem(as) disassociated himself from him. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَمَا كَانَ اسْتِغْفَارُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ لِأَبِيهِ إِلَّا عَن مَّوْعِدَةٍ وَعَدَهَا إِيَّاهُ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ أَنَّهُ عَدُوٌّ لِّلَّـهِ تَبَرَّأَ مِنْهُ ۚ إِنَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ لَأَوَّاهٌ حَلِيمٌ ١١٤﴾\nAnd the request of forgiveness of Abraham for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him. But when it became apparent to Abraham that his father was an enemy to Allah, he disassociated himself from him. Indeed was Abraham compassionate and patient.\n[At-Tawba: 114]\nThe Holy Quran also says:\n﴿قَدْ كَانَتْ لَكُمْ أُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ فِي إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَالَّذِينَ مَعَهُ إِذْ قَالُوا لِقَوْمِهِمْ إِنَّا بُرَآءُ مِنكُمْ وَمِمَّا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّـهِ كَفَرْنَا بِكُمْ وَبَدَا بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةُ وَالْبَغْضَاءُ أَبَدًا حَتَّىٰ تُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّـهِ وَحْدَهُ إِلَّا قَوْلَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ لِأَبِيهِ لَأَسْتَغْفِرَنَّ لَكَ وَمَا أَمْلِكُ لَكَ مِنَ اللَّـهِ مِن شَيْءٍ ۖ رَّبَّنَا عَلَيْكَ تَوَكَّلْنَا وَإِلَيْكَ أَنَبْنَا وَإِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيرُ ٤﴾\nThere has already been for you an excellent pattern in Abraham and those with him, when they said to their people, \"Indeed, we are disassociated from you and from whatever you worship other than Allah. We have denied you, and there has appeared between us and you animosity and hatred forever until you believe in Allah alone\" except for the saying of Abraham to his father, \"I will surely ask forgiveness for you, but I have not [power to do] for you anything against Allah. Our Lord, upon You we have relied, and to You we have returned, and to You is the destination.\n[Al-Mumtahina: 4]\nThe life of Ibraheem(as) is an excellent and noble example for us. In the path of Allah(swt) he even gave up his father who would not stop worshipping idols because anybody who commits ‘shirk’ is an enemy of Allah(swt) and ‘shirk’ is the greatest sin. [Luqman: 13]"],[59,"§Aziz-e-Misr\nAziz-e-Misr means the king of Misr. Aziz is one of the names of Allah(swt) but in the Holy Quran this word has been used in two places for the king of Egypt and in two places for prophet Yusuf(as) as follows:\n﴿وَقَالَ نِسْوَةٌ فِي الْمَدِينَةِ امْرَأَتُ الْعَزِيزِ تُرَاوِدُ فَتَاهَا عَن نَّفْسِهِ ۖ قَدْ شَغَفَهَا حُبًّا ۖ إِنَّا لَنَرَاهَا فِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٣٠﴾\nAnd women in the city said, \"The wife of al-'Azeez is seeking to seduce her slave boy; he has impassioned her with love. Indeed, we see her [to be] in clear error.\"\n[Yusuf: 30].\n﴿قَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُنَّ إِذْ رَاوَدتُّنَّ يُوسُفَ عَن نَّفْسِهِ ۚ قُلْنَ حَاشَ لِلَّـهِ مَا عَلِمْنَا عَلَيْهِ مِن سُوءٍ ۚ قَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ الْعَزِيزِ الْآنَ حَصْحَصَ الْحَقُّ أَنَا رَاوَدتُّهُ عَن نَّفْسِهِ وَإِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ ٥١﴾\nSaid [the king to the women], \"What was your condition when you sought to seduce Joseph?\" They said, \"Perfect is Allah! We know about him no evil.\" The wife of al-'Azeez said, \"Now the truth has become evident. It was I who sought to seduce him, and indeed, he is of the truthful.\n[Yusuf: 51]\nFrom the above verses it is evident that ‘Aziz’ is not the name of a particular individual but is the king, superintendent or in the modern times the prime minister of a country. In two other places ‘Aziz’ has been used for Yusuf(as). As to who this king of Egypt was, see ‘Yusuf’. In the Holy Bible, the name of this official is mentioned as ‘Potiphar’. (See Genesis 39:1). But the name of his wife is not mentioned in it. Some Muslim commentators are of the opinion that the wife’s name was ‘Zulekha’ but there is no proof of it."],[60,"§Ba’l\nBa’l is a word from the Sami language. It means ‘head’ or ‘chief’. Then, in Arabic the same word started being used for husband. Actually Ba’l was the name of one of the gods of the Canaanites, whom they worshipped. Then the Finiki people made it their god and when the Bani-Israel mingled with these people, they also started worshipping Ba’al. Then the worship of Ba’l spread to the whole of Palestine. After this the idol became popular under various names like Ba’l Shafu, Ba’l Jaboob, Ba’l Warnas, Ba’l Taamaar etc. Then a city was established in Damascus after Ba’l named ‘Ba’l Bak’. All these have been described in great detail in the Bible.\nProphet Ilyas(as) was sent by Allah(swt) to these people with the message to worship Allah(swt) alone:\n﴿وَإِنَّ إِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٢٣ إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ١٢٤ أَتَدْعُونَ بَعْلًا وَتَذَرُونَ أَحْسَنَ الْخَالِقِينَ ١٢٥ اللَّـهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ آبَائِكُمُ الْأَوَّلِينَ ١٢٦﴾\nAnd indeed, Elias was from among the messengers, When he said to his people, \"Will you not fear Allah? Do you call upon Ba'l and leave the best of creators - Allah, your Lord and the Lord of your first forefathers?\"\n[As-Saffat: 123-126]"],[61,"§Baabil(Babylon)\n‘Baabil’ is a word from the Akadi language which means ‘Door of Allah(swt).’ This is the name of an ancient city of Iraq which is situated between the two rivers Tigris and Euphrates, near the city of Hilla. It is about eighty kilometers from Baghdad. In 2000 B.C, this was the center of a vast empire. Bukht Nasar was one of the famous emperors of that empire. Between 605-562 B.C, he invaded Palestine, captured many Jews and brought them to Babylon as prisoners. After coming here, the Jews fell prey to many vices and became disobedient to Allah(swt). They even forgot their Hebrew language. A few scholars knew Hebrew. To bring back the Jews to the path of Allah(swt) many prophets were sent. Prominent among them was Daniel. He preached to them fervently but they were adamant and continued indulging their vices. Then Allah(swt) made them undergo a severe trial and sent the two angels ‘Harut’ and ‘Marut’ to them. The angels warned them that they had been sent as a test to them and that they could learn either good or bad things from them. But the Jews instead of learning good things from them learnt magic which could separate a man and his wife and thus became embroiled in trouble about which they had been warned. The Holy Quran describes this and the nature of Jews is also explained.\nIn 539 B.C, the Persian king Cyrus invaded Babylon. After the destruction of Babylon, the Jew Azra led the Jews back to Palestine. At that time the Jews harboured a great hatred for all human beings. In this state, Azra rewrote the Taurah and made additions making the Jews consider the other people as their slaves and allowing them to take reprisals whenever possible. As for Babylon, Alexander invaded it in 331 B.C. and destroyed Babylon completely. Till today Babylon remains in ruins. Archaeological diggings are still going on. Babylon is also famous for the tower of Babylon or the Tower of Babel which has seven stories. Babylon is described only once in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَاتَّبَعُوا مَا تَتْلُو الشَّيَاطِينُ عَلَىٰ مُلْكِ سُلَيْمَانَ ۖ وَمَا كَفَرَ سُلَيْمَانُ وَلَـٰكِنَّ الشَّيَاطِينَ كَفَرُوا يُعَلِّمُونَ النَّاسَ السِّحْرَ وَمَا أُنزِلَ عَلَى الْمَلَكَيْنِ بِبَابِلَ هَارُوتَ وَمَارُوتَ ۚ وَمَا يُعَلِّمَانِ مِنْ أَحَدٍ حَتَّىٰ يَقُولَا إِنَّمَا نَحْنُ فِتْنَةٌ فَلَا تَكْفُرْ ۖ فَيَتَعَلَّمُونَ مِنْهُمَا مَا يُفَرِّقُونَ بِهِ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَزَوْجِهِ ۚ وَمَا هُم بِضَارِّينَ بِهِ مِنْ أَحَدٍ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِ اللَّـهِ ۚ وَيَتَعَلَّمُونَ مَا يَضُرُّهُمْ وَلَا يَنفَعُهُمْ ۚ ١٠٢﴾\nAnd they followed [instead] what the devils had recited during the reign of Solomon. It was not Solomon who disbelieved, but the devils disbelieved, teaching people magic and that which was revealed to the two angels at Babylon, Harut and Marut. But the two angels do not teach anyone unless they say, \"We are a trial, so do not disbelieve [by practicing magic].\" And [yet] they learn from them that by which they cause separation between a man and his wife. But they do not harm anyone through it except by permission of Allah. And the people learn what harms them and does not benefit them.\n[Al-Baqara: 102]"],[62,"§Backbiting\nBackbiting means to speak ill about somebody behind their backs. This is a social evil and a disease which Islam vehemently forbids. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اجْتَنِبُوا كَثِيرًا مِّنَ الظَّنِّ إِنَّ بَعْضَ الظَّنِّ إِثْمٌ ۖ وَلَا تَجَسَّسُوا وَلَا يَغْتَب بَّعْضُكُم بَعْضًا ۚ أَيُحِبُّ أَحَدُكُمْ أَن يَأْكُلَ لَحْمَ أَخِيهِ مَيْتًا فَكَرِهْتُمُوهُ ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ تَوَّابٌ رَّحِيمٌ ١٢﴾\nO you who have believed, avoid much [negative] assumption. Indeed, some assumption is sin. And do not spy or backbite each other. Would one of you like to eat the flesh of his brother when dead? You would detest it. And fear Allah; indeed, Allah is Accepting of repentance and Merciful.\n[Al-Hujurat: 12]\nCriticising somebody behind their backs is very entertaining just as eating meat is enjoyable. But just as we find it disgusting to eat the flesh of our dead brother, we should abstain from speaking ill of our brother behind his back. Now it is for the person concerned to decide whether or not he would like to speak ill of his brother and eat his dead brother’s flesh. The analogy of the dead brother is given here because just as the dead brother cannot defend himself, the person who is being criticized cannot speak up for himself simply because he is not aware that something bad is being said about him. This is when the bad things being said about the person are true. And when the things being said about a person are untrue, then it is slander and an even greater sin. While exhorting the people to keep away from the social sins like backbiting, Islam also advocates love and affection for each other:\n﴿وَتَعَاوَنُوا عَلَى الْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوَىٰ ۖ وَلَا تَعَاوَنُوا عَلَى الْإِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ شَدِيدُ الْعِقَابِ ٢﴾\nAnd cooperate in righteousness and piety, but do not cooperate in sin and aggression. And fear Allah; indeed, Allah is severe in penalty.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 2]"],[63,"§Badr\nThis is the name of a valley which is situated at a distance of 175 kms from Madina on the route to Makka. A great battle had taken place there in which with the help of Allah(swt), Muslims emerged victorious. Allah(swt) describes it in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ نَصَرَكُمُ اللَّـهُ بِبَدْرٍ وَأَنتُمْ أَذِلَّةٌ ۖ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ ١٢٣﴾\nAnd already had Allah given you victory at [the battle of] Badr while you were few in number. Then fear Allah; perhaps you will be grateful.\n[Al-i-Imran: 123]\nThis was fought in 2 A.H, February, 623 A.D. The reason was that the disbelievers of Makka could not digest the fact Muhammad(saws) was living peacefully in Madina with his followers after migrating from Makka. So, under the leadership of Abu-Sufyan, a large group of traders were sent to Syria to bring back lots of wealth so that they could buy war equipment with it in order to forever finish off Muhammad(saws) and his followers. Muhammad(saws) got to know of this when the traders were returning to Makka and set out to attack them with a Muslim army of 313 soldiers. But Abu-Sufyan was a cunning leader. He got news about this and immediately sent a person named Zamzam to Makka and sought their help and protection. As the chiefs of Makka were already prepared to attack Madina, they set out for the attack with an army of one thousand. This was a new twist. The Muslims were about one-third in number and war-equipment. The Holy Prophet(saws) sought the opinion of his companions as to what was to be done? One person stood up and said that they should attack the traders. The Holy Prophet(saws) again sought their opinion. A few chiefs who understood the Holy Prophet(saws) stood up and said, “O Prophet of Allah(swt)! Do whatever Allah(swt) has instructed you, we are with you. We are not like the Bani-Israel who said to Musa(as) “You and your Lord fight in the war, we will stay back”. We shall say “You and your Lord fight in the war. We are with you.” This was the chief of the immigrants(Muhaajir) Miqdaad-bin-Amr. But the Holy Prophet(saws) wanted even the chiefs of Ansar to voice their opinion. So, he(saws) again asked for his companions’ advice. Then Saad-bin-Muaaz understood the situation and said, “O Prophet of Allah(swt)! You want our opinion?”. The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “Yes.” Then Saad-bin-Muaaz replied, “We have believed in you. We are with you. Even if you enter the ocean, we shall follow. Not even a single person will back off from among us(Ansar).” The Holy Prophet (saws) was pleased and declared jihad. This was a very difficult period in the history of Islam. A small army of 313 with very little war weapons set out to combat an army more than three times its size and moreover heavily equipped with arms and weapons. The situation was such that if those handful of soldiers had been defeated, there would not have been anyone left to sing the praises of Almighty Allah(swt).\nIn his commentary on the Holy Quran, the famous Islamic scholar Moulana Abdul-Kalam Azad says:\n“Sometimes a very trivial matter can turn a war either into a win or a defeat. With respect to the battle of Waterloo, the historians are unanimous in their opinion that if it hadn’t rained on the nights of 17th and 18th June 1815 A.D, Europe would have been different from what it is today because in that case Napoleon would not have waited till 12 O’clock for the ground to dry up and fighting would have started from dawn itself and Wellington would have been defeated before Gebhard Leberecht von Blücher, the Prussian commander arrived with his forces. In the same way, if the Muslims hadn’t emerged victorious in the battle of Badr, the future of Islam would’ve been different.”\nHence, this is what the Holy Prophet(saws) prayed to Allah(swt), “O Allah(swt)! If you cause my handful of army to be defeated, then there will not be anybody left on this earth who will exalt You.”\nThe Muslims triumphed in the Battle of Badr. Many powerful chiefs of Makka were killed and a new chapter in the history of Islam began. One whole surah ‘Al-Anfal’ was revealed in connection with this."],[64,"§Baheerah\nThe idol-worshippers of Makka were forever devising new ways and means to please their so-called gods and goddesses. One was that they would let go a she-camel in the name of some idol. They would not drink its milk saying that it was for that god. This animal was called Baheerah. Its ear would be split so that the people could distinguish it from the other camels. Nobody would milk it nor would anybody stop it from roaming about freely and grazing wherever it pleased. It was considered extremely sacred. The Holy Quran admonishes people against these sort of wrong practices:\n﴿مَا جَعَلَ اللَّـهُ مِن بَحِيرَةٍ وَلَا سَائِبَةٍ وَلَا وَصِيلَةٍ وَلَا حَامٍ ۙ وَلَـٰكِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يَفْتَرُونَ عَلَى اللَّـهِ الْكَذِبَ ۖ وَأَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُونَ ١٠٣﴾\nAllah has not appointed [such innovations as] bahirah or sa'ibah or wasilah or ham. But those who disbelieve invent falsehood about Allah, and most of them do not reason.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 103]"],[65,"§Baith\nBaith means to pledge or take oath. This is done by placing one’s hand on the other person’s hand and promising to help out each other. Breaking this pledge without a strong reason is a great sin. One of the Baiths is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿لَّقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّـهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ فَعَلِمَ مَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ فَأَنزَلَ السَّكِينَةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَأَثَابَهُمْ فَتْحًا قَرِيبًا ١٨﴾\nCertainly was Allah pleased with the believers when they pledged allegiance to you, [O Muhammad], under the tree, and He knew what was in their hearts, so He sent down tranquillity upon them and rewarded them with an imminent conquest .\n[Al-Fath: 18]\nThe reference is to the pledge which was taken at a place called Hudaibiya in 6 A.H. (For more details refer to ‘Fathe-Mubeen’)\nAllah(swt) commanded his Prophet(saws):\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ إِذَا جَاءَكَ الْمُؤْمِنَاتُ يُبَايِعْنَكَ عَلَىٰ أَن لَّا يُشْرِكْنَ بِاللَّـهِ شَيْئًا وَلَا يَسْرِقْنَ وَلَا يَزْنِينَ وَلَا يَقْتُلْنَ أَوْلَادَهُنَّ وَلَا يَأْتِينَ بِبُهْتَانٍ يَفْتَرِينَهُ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِنَّ وَأَرْجُلِهِنَّ وَلَا يَعْصِينَكَ فِي مَعْرُوفٍ ۙ فَبَايِعْهُنَّ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُنَّ اللَّـهَ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ١٢﴾\nO Prophet, when the believing women come to you pledging to you that they will not associate anything with Allah, nor will they steal, nor will they commit unlawful sexual intercourse, nor will they kill their children, nor will they bring forth a slander they have invented between their arms and legs, nor will they disobey you in what is right - then accept their pledge and ask forgiveness for them of Allah. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\n[Al-Mumtahina: 12]\nThis was the pledge taken from those women who had migrated to Madina. Or the native women of Madina who had reverted to Islam. These women would be made to take the pledge after reciting the ‘Kalima’ so that they would accept the other teachings of Islam with equal fervor. This pledge would be taken with the Holy Prophet(saws). After him, it was taken with the Caliphs and after them with the ruler of the state and a promise would also be made that they would follow his orders. There is no evidence of this pledge being taken with anybody else."],[66,"§Bani-Israel\nBani-Israel means the progeny or descendants of Israel. Israel is the title of Yaqub-bin-Ishaq, the grandson of Ibraheem(as), which means ‘the one who fights jihad with Allah(swt)’ (see Genesis 32:28). The tribe which was procreated with his twelve sons is the ‘Bani-Israel’. Allah(swt) bestowed many favors on the Bani-Israel which are mentioned again and again in the Holy Quran. A few of them are:\n﴿يَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتِيَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَأَنِّي فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ ٤٧﴾\nThey were preferred over other people of those times. (See Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-47)\n﴿وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ الْكِتَابَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ وَرَزَقْنَاهُم مِّنَ الطَّيِّبَاتِ وَفَضَّلْنَاهُمْ عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ ١٦﴾\nSecondly, they were given prophethood and were made the rulers. (See Surah-45, Al-Jathiya, Verse-16)\n﴿وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا مُوسَى الْهُدَىٰ وَأَوْرَثْنَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ الْكِتَابَ ٥٣ هُدًى وَذِكْرَىٰ لِأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ ٥٤﴾\nThirdly, they were given the Scripture for their guidance. (See Surah-40, Al-Momin, Verses-53,54)\n﴿وَلَمَّا جَاءَهُمْ كِتَابٌ مِّنْ عِندِ اللَّـهِ مُصَدِّقٌ لِّمَا مَعَهُمْ وَكَانُوا مِن قَبْلُ يَسْتَفْتِحُونَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فَلَمَّا جَاءَهُم مَّا عَرَفُوا كَفَرُوا بِهِ ۚ فَلَعْنَةُ اللَّـهِ عَلَى الْكَافِرِينَ ٨٩﴾\nThis Scripture or book contained the good news of the coming of the Last Prophet(saws), but when he came they rejected him(saws). (See Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-89)\nIn fact Allah(swt) had made it clear in the book that they would cause corruption on the earth twice and it will be too much and both the times they would be destroyed. And if they continue doing mischief, then the result would be the same as before.\n﴿وَقَضَيْنَا إِلَىٰ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ فِي الْكِتَابِ لَتُفْسِدُنَّ فِي الْأَرْضِ مَرَّتَيْنِ وَلَتَعْلُنَّ عُلُوًّا كَبِيرًا ٤ فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ أُولَاهُمَا بَعَثْنَا عَلَيْكُمْ عِبَادًا لَّنَا أُولِي بَأْسٍ شَدِيدٍ فَجَاسُوا خِلَالَ الدِّيَارِ ۚ وَكَانَ وَعْدًا مَّفْعُولًا ٥ ثُمَّ رَدَدْنَا لَكُمُ الْكَرَّةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَأَمْدَدْنَاكُم بِأَمْوَالٍ وَبَنِينَ وَجَعَلْنَاكُمْ أَكْثَرَ نَفِيرًا ٦ إِنْ أَحْسَنتُمْ أَحْسَنتُمْ لِأَنفُسِكُمْ ۖ وَإِنْ أَسَأْتُمْ فَلَهَا ۚ فَإِذَا جَاءَ وَعْدُ الْآخِرَةِ لِيَسُوءُوا وُجُوهَكُمْ وَلِيَدْخُلُوا الْمَسْجِدَ كَمَا دَخَلُوهُ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَلِيُتَبِّرُوا مَا عَلَوْا تَتْبِيرًا ٧﴾\nعَسَىٰ رَبُّكُمْ أَن يَرْحَمَكُمْ ۚ وَإِنْ عُدتُّمْ عُدْنَا ۘ وَجَعَلْنَا جَهَنَّمَ لِلْكَافِرِينَ حَصِيرًا\nAnd We conveyed to the Children of Israel in the Scripture that, \"You will surely cause corruption on the earth twice, and you will surely reach [a degree of] great haughtiness. So when the [time of] promise came for the first of them, We sent against you servants of Ours - those of great military might, and they probed [even] into the homes, and it was a promise fulfilled. Then We gave back to you a return victory over them. And We reinforced you with wealth and sons and made you more numerous in manpower [And said], \"If you do good, you do good for yourselves; and if you do evil, [you do it] to yourselves.\" Then when the final promise came, [We sent your enemies] to sadden your faces and to enter the temple in Jerusalem, as they entered it the first time, and to destroy what they had taken over with [total] destruction. [Then Allah said], \"It is expected, [if you repent], that your Lord will have mercy upon you. But if you return [to sin], We will return [to punishment]. And We have made Hell, for the disbelievers, a prison-bed.\"\n[Bani-Israel: 4-8]\nIn the Taurah, the prophets had warned the Bani-Israel again and again not to worship anyone other than Allah(swt) and not to throw the book of Allah(swt) behind their backs or else they would have to face the wrath of Allah(swt). But the Bani-Israel did not heed their warnings as a result of which they were faced with two great devastations:\nThe first devastation: The king of Babylon ‘Bukht Nasar’ attacked Baitul-Muqaddas four times between 605 and 582 B.C, killing and capturing thousands and taking them away to Babylon. He also destroyed the place of worship of Sulaiman(as) and till today its exact location is not known. In the book ‘Kings’ of the Holy Bible, a detailed description of the attacks of Bukht Nasar is given.\nThe second devastation: In 70 A.D, the Roman king Titus attacked Jerusalem and killed more than a lakh Jews and took away more than seven thousand as prisoners to his country, a few of whom were sent to Egypt as slaves. After this attack, Jewish kingdom could never be established again. In the twentieth century A.D, the Jews were exiled from Europe and settled in Palestine and in 1948 A.D, the Jewish state was formed. Now we should just wait and watch as to how long this will exist as Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nعَسَىٰ رَبُّكُمْ أَن يَرْحَمَكُمْ ۚ وَإِنْ عُدتُّمْ عُدْنَا\n[Then Allah said], \"It is expected, [if you repent], that your Lord will have mercy upon you. But if you return [to sin], We will return [to punishment].\n[Bani-Israel: 8]\nThis is a very brief history of Bani-Israel. So much has been written about them in the Holy Quran that history is actually redundant.\nإِنَّ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنَ يَقُصُّ عَلَىٰ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ أَكْثَرَ الَّذِي هُمْ فِيهِ يَخْتَلِفُونَ\nIndeed, this Qur'an relates to the Children of Israel most of that over which they disagree.\n[An-Naml: 76]\nFor more information see ‘Musa(as)’."],[67,"§Barren\nBarren means ‘Aqeem’ in Arabic which means unproductive; for example a desert.\nIn the Holy Quran, this word has been used in three contexts:\nThe popular meaning is a woman unable to conceive. This can be due to two reasons. The first one is that Allah(swt) has created her this way as it says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿يَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ إِنَاثًا وَيَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ الذُّكُورَ ٤٩ أَوْ يُزَوِّجُهُمْ ذُكْرَانًا وَإِنَاثًا ۖ وَيَجْعَلُ مَن يَشَاءُ عَقِيمًا ۚ إِنَّهُ عَلِيمٌ قَدِيرٌ ٥٠﴾\nHe gives to whom He wills female [children], and He gives to whom He wills males. Or He makes them [both] males and females, and He renders whom He wills barren.\n[Ash-Shura: 49, 50]\nIf it is so, then no saint, sanyasi, pious person, sahib or some grave or anybody for that matter has any power to make her conceive. And the people who go to these sort of people and to the graves are in fact rejecting the Sovereignty of Allah(swt). This is actually ‘shirk’ which was widely prevalent in the pre-Islamic days and is still in existence in many places.\nOnly Allah(swt) has the power to grant children to these barren women in some miraculous way.\nFor example when Ibraheem(as) was given the good news about a wise son, his wife beat her face in surprise and said:\n﴿فَأَقْبَلَتِ امْرَأَتُهُ فِي صَرَّةٍ فَصَكَّتْ وَجْهَهَا وَقَالَتْ عَجُوزٌ عَقِيمٌ ٢٩ قَالُوا كَذَٰلِكِ قَالَ رَبُّكِ ۖ إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْحَكِيمُ الْعَلِيمُ ٣٠﴾\nAnd his wife approached with a cry [of alarm] and struck her face and said, \"[I am] a barren old woman!\" They said, \"Thus has said your Lord; indeed, He is the Wise, the Knowing.\"\n[Adh-Dhariyat: 29-30]\nIn the same sense the word ‘Aakhir’ has also been used in the Holy Quran to mean ‘barren’. It means ‘to cut off’ that is a barren woman has children ‘cut off’ from her. As is mentioned in the case of Zachariah:\n﴿كهيعص ١ ذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهُ زَكَرِيَّا ٢ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ نِدَاءً خَفِيًّا ٣ قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّي وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّأْسُ شَيْبًا وَلَمْ أَكُن بِدُعَائِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا ٤ وَإِنِّي خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِيَ مِن وَرَائِي وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَتِي عَاقِرًا فَهَبْ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ وَلِيًّا ٥ يَرِثُنِي وَيَرِثُ مِنْ آلِ يَعْقُوبَ ۖ وَاجْعَلْهُ رَبِّ رَضِيًّا ٦ يَا زَكَرِيَّا إِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلَامٍ اسْمُهُ يَحْيَىٰ لَمْ نَجْعَل لَّهُ مِن قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا ٧ قَالَ رَبِّ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي غُلَامٌ وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَتِي عَاقِرًا وَقَدْ بَلَغْتُ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ عِتِيًّا ٨ قَالَ كَذَٰلِكَ قَالَ رَبُّكَ هُوَ عَلَيَّ هَيِّنٌ وَقَدْ خَلَقْتُكَ مِن قَبْلُ وَلَمْ تَكُ شَيْئًا ٩﴾\nKaf, Ha, Ya, 'Ayn, Sad. [This is] a mention of the mercy of your Lord to His servant Zechariah. When he called to his Lord a private supplication. He said, \"My Lord, indeed my bones have weakened, and my head has filled with white, and never have I been in my supplication to You, my Lord, unhappy. And indeed, I fear the successors after me, and my wife has been barren, so give me from Yourself an heir. Who will inherit me and inherit from the family of Jacob. And make him, my Lord, pleasing [to You].\" [He was told], \"O Zechariah, indeed We give you good tidings of a boy whose name will be John. We have not assigned to any before [this] name.\" He said, \"My Lord, how will I have a boy when my wife has been barren and I have reached extreme old age?\" [An angel] said, \"Thus [it will be]; your Lord says, 'It is easy for Me, for I created you before, while you were nothing.' \"\n[Maryam: 1-9]\nThat is, it is not difficult for Allah(swt) to grant offspring to a barren woman.\nThe second reason is that even though the woman was not created barren, due to some reason she is unable to conceive. In this case she should be treated by some doctor because Allah(swt) has created a cure for every disease. It is the task of the doctor to diagnose the disease and treat it accordingly.\nNow we can clearly understand that in both the cases, no saint or sanyasi can do anything. They just lure and dupe innocent and foolish people.\nThe wind which blows without clouds is also called ‘Reeh Akheem’. This not only causes destruction but is also useless for farming. Such a wind was sent towards the tribe of Aad and it destroyed them.\nA day which does not bring happiness but only causes sorrow is also called ‘Akeem’. [Al-Hajj: 55]"],[68,"§Barzakh\nBarzakh has been described in three places in the Holy Quran:\nFirst:\n﴿حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَاءَ أَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ رَبِّ ارْجِعُونِ ٩٩ لَعَلِّي أَعْمَلُ صَالِحًا فِيمَا تَرَكْتُ ۚ كَلَّا ۚ إِنَّهَا كَلِمَةٌ هُوَ قَائِلُهَا ۖ وَمِن وَرَائِهِم بَرْزَخٌ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ ١٠٠﴾\n[For such is the state of the disbelievers], until, when death comes to one of them, he says, \"My Lord, send me back. That I might do righteousness in that which I left behind.\" No! It is only a word he is saying; and behind them is a barrier until the Day they are resurrected.\n[Al-Mu’minun: 99, 100]\nThis means that when the disobedient people are about to die, they pray to Allah(swt) to send them back to the world which they are about to leave so that they can earn His pleasure by performing pious deeds. That is, in the face of death they become believers in Allah(swt). Allah(swt) says that it is a lie as they would repeat their sins even if He(swt) sends them back. At another place in the Holy Quran it says:\nوَلَوْ رُدُّوا لَعَادُوا لِمَا نُهُوا عَنْهُ وَإِنَّهُمْ لَكَاذِبُونَ\nAnd even if they were returned, they would return to that which they were forbidden; and indeed, they are liars.\n[Al-An’am: 28]\nAnd this is what every sinner says when he is dying. But nobody was ever sent back to earth. They will stay in ‘Barzakh’ till the Day of Resurrection. Some scholars say that ‘Barzakh’ means the grave. They are of the opinion that men stay in their graves till Doomsday and after that they shall either go to heaven or hell depending on their deeds.\nSecond:\n﴿مَرَجَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ يَلْتَقِيَانِ ١٩ بَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخٌ لَّا يَبْغِيَانِ ٢٠﴾\nHe released the two seas, meeting [side by side]; Between them is a barrier [so] neither of them transgresses.\n[Ar-Rahman: 19, 20]\nThe literal meaning of ‘Barzakh’ is a barrier between two things. Even a small piece of land between two seas is called ‘Barzakh’. That is why the transitory life between this worldly life and the life of the Hereafter is called ‘Barzakh’. The people living in Barzakh can neither be counted among the people of this earth nor among the people of the hereafter.\nThird:\nAt another place in the Holy Quran, it has been described as follows:\nوَهُوَ الَّذِي مَرَجَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ هَٰذَا عَذْبٌ فُرَاتٌ وَهَٰذَا مِلْحٌ أُجَاجٌ وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخًا وَحِجْرًا مَّحْجُورًا\nAnd it is He who has released [simultaneously] the two seas, one fresh and sweet and one salty and bitter, and He placed between them a barrier and prohibiting partition.\n[Al-Furqan: 53]\nEven here ‘Barzakh’ has been used in its literal sense which means a barrier or partition because at various places in the oceans, there are springs of fresh and sweet water which though existing in the middle of salty waters do not mix with it. The reason is that Allah(swt) has placed a barrier between these two types of water which we cannot see.\nAfter explaining the various signs, Allah(swt) says that man is so wicked that in spite of all the comforts which Allah(swt) has given him, he worships those which can neither harm nor benefit him. Allah(swt) says in the succeeding verses of surah Al-Furqan:\n﴿وَهُوَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ مِنَ الْمَاءِ بَشَرًا فَجَعَلَهُ نَسَبًا وَصِهْرًا ۗ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ قَدِيرًا ٥٤ وَيَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ مَا لَا يَنفَعُهُمْ وَلَا يَضُرُّهُمْ ۗ وَكَانَ الْكَافِرُ عَلَىٰ رَبِّهِ ظَهِيرًا ٥٥﴾\nAnd it is He who has created from water a human being and made him [a relative by] lineage and marriage. And ever is your Lord competent [concerning creation]. But they worship rather than Allah that which does not benefit them or harm them, and the disbeliever is ever, against his Lord, an assistant [to Satan].\n[Al-Furqan: 54, 55]"],[69,"§Begging\nThe main pillar of Islam is ‘Tawheed’ or ‘monotheism’. It is wrong to ask anything from anybody other than Allah(swt) because when He(swt) is the one providing livelihood for everybody, then why should we ask anything from others? Whatever we need, we should ask Allah(swt) alone. When we ask Him, He(swt) will make some arrangement for us. We have only been commanded to follow the straight path. Even while earning our livelihood, we are commanded to stick to the path of truth. It is forbidden to earn our livelihood through wrong means. That is why begging to earn one’s livelihood has been severely criticized both in the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith.\nAllah(swt) has praised those people who do not ask for anything persistently and they are the ones who deserve the ‘zakat’. We should actually seek out such people and give zakat to them. Zakat is rightfully theirs.\nلِلْفُقَرَاءِ الَّذِينَ أُحْصِرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ لَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ ضَرْبًا فِي الْأَرْضِ يَحْسَبُهُمُ الْجَاهِلُ أَغْنِيَاءَ مِنَ التَّعَفُّفِ تَعْرِفُهُم بِسِيمَاهُمْ لَا يَسْأَلُونَ النَّاسَ إِلْحَافًا ۗ وَمَا تُنفِقُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ بِهِ عَلِيمٌ\n[Charity is] for the poor who have been restricted for the cause of Allah, unable to move about in the land. An ignorant [person] would think them self-sufficient because of their restraint, but you will know them by their [characteristic] sign. They do not ask people persistently [or at all]. And whatever you spend of good - indeed, Allah is Knowing of it.\n[Al-Baqara: 273]\nAccording to a Sahih Hadith:\n“The hand above is better than the hand below, the hand above is the one which gives, and the hand below is the one which accepts.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1429, Sahih Muslim, 1033)\nAccording to another Sahih Hadith, the Holy Prophet(saws) said after swearing:\n“If one were to take his rope and collect wood, then sell it and eat and give in charity whatever he earns from it, it is better than going to somebody and asking him for something. The person may or may not give him something.”\n(Bukhari, 1470 and Muslim, 1042)\nA companion named Sauban narrates that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“Who will make a promise in return for paradise?” Sauban said, “I promise.” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Never ask anything from anybody.”\nIt is written about Sauban that even if his whip fell down, he would not ask anybody to pick it up, but he would climb down from his horse and pick it up himself.\n(Musnad Ahmad, 5:217, Ibn-Maaja-1837, Nasai 5:96)\nAccording to another Sahih Hadith:\n“Anybody who asks (begs) from others in order to increase his wealth has actually asked for a ball of fire. Now let whosoever wants increase his wealth or decrease it.”\n(Sahih Muslim 1041)\nThat is, let him ask for the ball of fire and increase his wealth or decrease it by not asking and this ball of fire is the ball of hell.\nBut if anybody gets something without asking for it, then it is better to accept it. According to a sahih hadith, when one day the Holy Prophet(saws) gave something to Umar(ra), he replied, “O Prophet of Allah(swt)! Give this to somebody who is poorer than me.” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied,\n“Take this. Accept the wealth which comes to you without you asking for it and without any greed and do not covet whatever you do not get.”\n(Bukhari, 1473 and Muslim, 1045)\nAccording to another sahih hadith, addressing Hakeem-bin-Hizam, the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“O Hakeem! This is some money and fresh sweet, so whoever accepts it without any greed shall be rewarded with an increase in his wealth and whoever accepts it with greed shall have no increase in wealth.”\n(Bukhari, 1472 and Muslim 1035)\nAccording to another hadith:\n“If somebody gets something from his brother without asking and without any greed, it is his livelihood from Allah(swt).”\n(Musnad Ahmad, 17936)\nThe Holy Quran while condemning begging also has some rules for the people who give charity. A few of them are as follows:\nDo not speak harshly to the beggar:\nوَأَمَّا السَّائِلَ فَلَا تَنْهَرْ\nAnd as for the petitioner, do not repel [him].\n[Az-Zuha: 10]\nThat is, while begging is definitely wrong, it is a bigger sin to treat the beggar harshly.\nIt is not good to make the beggar go away empty-handed:\nAccording to a sahih hadith, the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Save yourselves from hell-fire, be it even by giving a piece of date in charity.”\n(Bukhari, 1417 and Muslim, 1:16)\nIslam is one religion which lays great stress on love and brotherhood among all people. That is why the Holy Quran commands us again and again to spend in the path of Allah(swt). Along with salah it exhorts us to give zakat also. The Holy Prophet(saws) explains various ways and means to escape the punishment of hell-fire. One of them is to spend money on one’s relatives, orphans and the needy. This is the way to earn the pleasure of Allah(swt) and the abode of the one who earns Allah(swt)’s pleasure is paradise.\nTherefore, we should never let a person who asks us for something go away empty-handed; we should give him something or the other be it the roasted leg of some animal.\n(Abu Dawood, 1666, Tirmizi, 665, Nasai, 257)\nThe truly needy is the one who does not question:\nAccording to one sahih hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said, “The truly needy is not the one who goes door to door begging for one-one or two-two morsels of food or one-one or two-two dates.” The people asked, ”O Prophet of Allah(swt)! Then who is really poor?” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “The really poor is the one who does not ask questions. Looking at him we cannot guess that he is poor. Nor does he spread his hands in front of others for asking.”\n(Bukhari, 1479 and Muslim 1039)\nSo, we must seek out such people who actually deserve zakat, charity, etc.\nThe people who go around begging do not actually deserve alms and charity as they have taken up begging to avoid hard work. Islam emphasizes the importance of hard work and earning one’s livelihood in the right way. If even after this, he cannot make ends meet, then he can accept zakat and charity."],[70,"§Betrayal\nAllah(swt) does not like traitors or the people who betray whether they are Muslims or non-Muslims. After entering some treaty or signing a pact, if one of the sides breaks it, it is termed betrayal. If there is fear of betrayal, then the treaty should be broken from both the sides or else it will incur the displeasure of Allah(swt). (See Surah-8, Al-Anfal, Verse-58)\nWe can understand from this that the Holy Quran lays great stress on truth in every aspect of life including wars."],[71,"§Biddat\nDeviating from the basic teachings of Islam and including our own concepts in religion is termed ‘biddat.’ The followers of the religions before Islam did just this as is mentioned in the Holy Quran:\nوَرَهْبَانِيَّةً ابْتَدَعُوهَا مَا كَتَبْنَاهَا عَلَيْهِمْ إِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ رِضْوَانِ اللَّهِ فَمَا رَعَوْهَا حَقَّ رِعَايَتِهَا\nmonasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them except [that they did so] seeking the approval of Allah.\n[Al-Hadid: 27]\nIn the above verse it is mentioned that those religious people gave up all worldly life and became monks and this is what they themselves invented in order to please Allah(swt). But Allah(swt) makes it clear that the pleasure of Allah(swt) cannot be obtained by such innovations however pleasing they may be. The pleasure of Allah(swt) can only be obtained by following His(swt) commands. That is why the Holy Prophet(saws) has severely criticized the people who do biddat. According to a sahih hadith:\n\"If somebody innovates something which is not present in our religion, then that thing will be rejected.\"\n(Bukhari, 2697 and Muslim, 1718)\nAccording to another sahih hadith:\n“Every biddat leads one astray.”\n(See Sahih Muslim, 867)\nThat is why the Muslims held on firmly to the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith. They did not introduce innovations and preached the same to the others. That is why the Islamic teachings are still the same as they were during the time of the Holy Prophet(saws) and subsequently during the time of his companions and shall remain so till the Last Day and the bidaat of the innovators will be rejected. So, the people who from time to time keep introducing new things better fear Allah(swt) because their bidaat will not harm Islam in any way but their Hereafter will surely be ruined."],[72,"§Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem\n‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’ means ‘In the name of Allah, the Most Beneficent, the Most Merciful’. Before beginning any task, it is necessary to say ‘Bismillah’. Except Surah-9, At-Tawba, every surah begins with this kalima. So, a few scholars are of the opinion that ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’ is the first verse of every surah. That is why ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’ should be said before reciting any surah except the surah At-Tawba. And the scholars who feel that this is not the first verse say that ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’ should be recited silently. But everyone is agreed on the fact that ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’ is a verse of Surah-27, An-Naml, because Sulaiman(as) begins his letter to the Queen of Sheba with ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’:\n﴿قَالَتْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ إِنِّي أُلْقِيَ إِلَيَّ كِتَابٌ كَرِيمٌ ٢٩ إِنَّهُ مِن سُلَيْمَانَ وَإِنَّهُ بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ ٣٠﴾\nShe said, \"O eminent ones, indeed, to me has been delivered a noble letter. Indeed, it is from Solomon, and indeed, it reads: 'In the name of Allah, the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful.'\n[An-Naml: 29, 30]\nIn the same way, after building the ark, Nuh(as) said to the people:\nوَقَالَ ارْكَبُوا فِيهَا بِسْمِ اللَّهِ مَجْرَاهَا وَمُرْسَاهَا ۚ\nAnd [Noah] said, \"Embark therein; in the name of Allah is its course and its anchorage.\"\n[Hud: 41]\nIt is narrated in the sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) always said ‘Bismillah’ before beginning any task and also asked his companions to do the same. One day someone sent some food to the Holy Prophet(saws). Umar-bin-Abi Salma, the son of his wife Umm-e-Salma was with him. He(saws) started eating, picking his food from here and there on the plate. Seeing this the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“O Child! Take the name of Allah(swt), eat with your right hand and eat from whatever is near you.”\n(Bukhari 5376 and Muslim, 2022)\nTake the name of Allah(swt) means to begin by saying ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’.\nWhile telling us that we should begin by saying ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’, this hadith also explains the Islamic etiquettes of eating.\nIf someone forgets to say ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’ before commencing some task, he should say it whenever he remembers. Whatever task is done by first reciting ‘Bismillah-hir-Rehman-nir-Raheem’ becomes blessed and fruitful and according to a popular hadith anything begun without taking the name of Allah(swt) will be incomplete and not beneficial.\nIn the same way it is compulsory to take the name of Allah(swt) before slaughtering an animal; if not, it is forbidden to eat it:\nوَلَا تَأْكُلُوا مِمَّا لَمْ يُذْكَرِ اسْمُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ وَإِنَّهُ لَفِسْقٌ\nAnd do not eat of that upon which the name of Allah has not been mentioned, for indeed, it is grave disobedience.\n[Al-An’am: 121]\nAnd it is also mentioned:\nفَكُلُوا مِمَّا ذُكِرَ اسْمُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ إِن كُنتُم بِآيَاتِهِ مُؤْمِنِينَ\nSo eat of that [meat] upon which the name of Allah has been mentioned, if you are believers in His verses.\n[Al-An’am: 118]\n“It is compulsory for the Muslims to recite Bismillah before slaughtering an animal. If the name of Allah(swt) is not pronounced, then the meat of that animal is forbidden. But if there is a doubt whether the name of Allah(swt) has been pronounced or not, then the Holy Prophet(saws) instructed that we should pronounce the name of Allah(swt) and eat it.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5507)"],[73,"§Biyah\n‘Biyah’ is the plural of ‘Biatun’ which means the church of the Christians. It is the rule of Allah(swt) that He(swt) keeps replacing one group of people with the others. If it hadn’t been so, then these monasteries, churches, worship-places of the Jews, mosques of the Muslims which are the places of worshipping and remembering Allah(swt) would have been felled and this earth would have been a place of utter chaos and destruction and would have ceased to exist before the Last Day.\nWith reference to this, it says in the Holy Quran:\nالَّذِينَ أُخْرِجُوا مِن دِيَارِهِم بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ إِلَّا أَن يَقُولُوا رَبُّنَا اللَّهُ ۗ وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ اللَّهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُم بِبَعْضٍ لَّهُدِّمَتْ صَوَامِعُ وَبِيَعٌ وَصَلَوَاتٌ وَمَسَاجِدُ يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا اسْمُ اللَّهِ كَثِيرًا ۗ\n[They are] those who have been evicted from their homes without right - only because they say, \"Our Lord is Allah.\" And were it not that Allah checks the people, some by means of others, there would have been demolished monasteries, churches, synagogues, and mosques in which the name of Allah is much mentioned.\n[Al-Hajj: 40]"],[74,"§Blood\nIt is forbidden to drink blood. It says at one place in the Holy Quran:\nإِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَيْتَةَ وَالدَّمَ وَلَحْمَ الْخِنزِيرِ وَمَا أُهِلَّ بِهِ لِغَيْرِ اللَّهِ ۖ\nHe has only forbidden to you dead animals, blood, the flesh of swine, and that which has been dedicated to other than Allah.\n[Al-Baqara: 173]\nThat is why it is necessary that the animal be slaughtered in the correct Islamic way so that the blood flows out. It is forbidden to eat the flesh of animals slaughtered using electric shock or killed in one shot (jhatka) or which have died from natural causes because in all these cases the blood does not flow out and this blood which remains in the body breeds disease-causing micro-organisms."],[75,"§Breastfeeding\nSee ‘Riza’at’."],[76,"§Calf\nCalf or the young cow has been used for sacrifice and eating purposes since ancient times.\nWhen the angels came to Ibraheem(as) to give him the good news about a pious son, he thought they were guests and immediately went in and brought a roasted calf and placed it in front of them:\n﴿فَرَاغَ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِهِ فَجَاءَ بِعِجْلٍ سَمِينٍ ٢٦ فَقَرَّبَهُ إِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ أَلَا تَأْكُلُونَ ٢٧﴾\nThen he went to his family and came with a fat [roasted] calf. And placed it near them; he said, \"Will you not eat?\"\n[Adh-Dhariyat: 26, 27]\nAs the polytheists made idols of things which were useful to them and worshipped them, they made an idol of the calf. The Egyptians also made an idol of the calf which was called ‘Abees’. Influenced by them, the Bani-Israel also made an idol of the calf when Musa(as) went to Mount Tur to get the Taurah:\nوَإِذْ وَاعَدْنَا مُوسَىٰ أَرْبَعِينَ لَيْلَةً ثُمَّ اتَّخَذْتُمُ الْعِجْلَ مِن بَعْدِهِ وَأَنتُمْ ظَالِمُونَ\nAnd [recall] when We made an appointment with Moses for forty nights. Then you took [for worship] the calf after him, while you were wrongdoers.\n[Al-Baqara: 51]\nوَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِ يَا قَوْمِ إِنَّكُمْ ظَلَمْتُمْ أَنفُسَكُم بِاتِّخَاذِكُمُ الْعِجْلَ\nAnd [recall] when Moses said to his people, \"O my people, indeed you have wronged yourselves by your taking of the calf [for worship].\n[Al-Baqara: 54]\nوَلَقَدْ جَاءَكُم مُّوسَىٰ بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ ثُمَّ اتَّخَذْتُمُ الْعِجْلَ مِن بَعْدِهِ وَأَنتُمْ ظَالِمُونَ\nAnd Moses had certainly brought you clear proofs. Then you took the calf [in worship] after that, while you were wrongdoers.\n[Al-Baqara: 92]\nثُمَّ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ مِن بَعْدِ مَا جَاءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّنَاتُ فَعَفَوْنَا عَن ذَٰلِكَ ۚ\nThen they took the calf [for worship] after clear evidences had come to them, and We pardoned that.\n[An-Nisa: 153]\nMusa(as), who like all other prophets had come with the message of Tawheed was furious when he found his tribe worshipping the calf which they themselves had made. Before going to Mount Tur, he had made his brother Haroon(as), who was also a prophet, his representative. So, angry at both his brother and his tribe Bani-Israel, he started pulling his brother by his head:\nوَلَمَّا رَجَعَ مُوسَىٰ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ غَضْبَانَ أَسِفًا قَالَ بِئْسَمَا خَلَفْتُمُونِي مِن بَعْدِي ۖ أَعَجِلْتُمْ أَمْرَ رَبِّكُمْ ۖ وَأَلْقَى الْأَلْوَاحَ وَأَخَذَ بِرَأْسِ أَخِيهِ يَجُرُّهُ إِلَيْهِ ۚ قَالَ ابْنَ أُمَّ إِنَّ الْقَوْمَ اسْتَضْعَفُونِي وَكَادُوا يَقْتُلُونَنِي فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِيَ الْأَعْدَاءَ وَلَا تَجْعَلْنِي مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ\nAnd when Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved, he said, \"How wretched is that by which you have replaced me after [my departure]. Were you impatient over the matter of your Lord?\" And he threw down the tablets and seized his brother by [the hair of] his head, pulling him toward him. [Aaron] said, \"O son of my mother, indeed the people oppressed me and were about to kill me, so let not the enemies rejoice over me and do not place me among the wrongdoing people.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 150]\nWe come to know from this that Haroon(as) did not give the Bani-Israel permission to worship the calf, but fearing some harm from them he just kept quiet. He also feared that if he were tough, it might cause disunity among the Bani-Israel as is mentioned in the Holy Quran:\nقَالَ يَا ابْنَ أُمَّ لَا تَأْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِي وَلَا بِرَأْسِي ۖ إِنِّي خَشِيتُ أَن تَقُولَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِي\n[Aaron] said, \"O son of my mother, do not seize [me] by my beard or by my head. Indeed, I feared that you would say, 'You caused division among the Children of Israel, and you did not observe [or await] my word.' \"\n[Ta-Ha: 94]\nFrom the above verse of the Holy Quran it is clear that it was not Haroon(as) who made and worshipped the calf as is mentioned in the Bible. The Bible says that Haroon(as) collected the gold ear-rings of the women of Bani-Israel and then made the gold calf and said:\nSo all the people took off their earrings and brought them to Aaron. He took what they handed him and made it into an idol cast in the shape of a calf, fashioning it with a tool. Then they said, “These are your gods, Israel, who brought you up out of Egypt.” When Aaron saw this, he built an altar in front of the calf and announced, “Tomorrow there will be a festival to the Lord.”\n(Bible, Exodus, 32:4-6)\nThe truth is that the man who made the idol was called ‘Samiri’ whose description is given in the Holy Quran. Most of the commentators believe him to be a hypocrite who would try to mislead the believers from the tribe of Bani-Israel. We do not have much information regarding this. Anyway he was an idol-worshipper who had somehow managed to come to come from Egypt to Sinai with Musa(as) where he had stayed for forty years along with his tribe. Musa(as) also had an argument with Samiri:\n﴿قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يَا سَامِرِيُّ ٩٥ قَالَ بَصُرْتُ بِمَا لَمْ يَبْصُرُوا بِهِ فَقَبَضْتُ قَبْضَةً مِّنْ أَثَرِ الرَّسُولِ فَنَبَذْتُهَا وَكَذَٰلِكَ سَوَّلَتْ لِي نَفْسِي ٩٦ قَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَإِنَّ لَكَ فِي الْحَيَاةِ أَن تَقُولَ لَا مِسَاسَ ۖ وَإِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّن تُخْلَفَهُ ۖ وَانظُرْ إِلَىٰ إِلَٰهِكَ الَّذِي ظَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفًا ۖ لَّنُحَرِّقَنَّهُ ثُمَّ لَنَنسِفَنَّهُ فِي الْيَمِّ نَسْفًا ٩٧ إِنَّمَا إِلَٰهُكُمُ اللَّهُ الَّذِي لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ وَسِعَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا ٩٨﴾\n[Moses] said, \"And what is your case, O Samiri?\" He said, \"I saw what they did not see, so I took a handful [of dust] from the track of the messenger and threw it, and thus did my soul entice me.\" [Moses] said, \"Then go. And indeed, it is [decreed] for you in [this] life to say, 'No contact.' And indeed, you have an appointment [in the Hereafter] you will not fail to keep. And look at your 'god' to which you remained devoted. We will surely burn it and blow it into the sea with a blast. Your god is only Allah, except for whom there is no deity. He has encompassed all things in knowledge.\"\n[Ta-Ha: 95-98]\nIn this way the Bani-Israel became devoted to the calf and could not stop themselves from worshipping it:\nوَإِذْ أَخَذْنَا مِيثَاقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ الطُّورَ خُذُوا مَا آتَيْنَاكُم بِقُوَّةٍ وَاسْمَعُوا ۖ قَالُوا سَمِعْنَا وَعَصَيْنَا وَأُشْرِبُوا فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ الْعِجْلَ بِكُفْرِهِمْ ۚ قُلْ بِئْسَمَا يَأْمُرُكُم بِهِ إِيمَانُكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ\nAnd [recall] when We took your covenant and raised over you the mount, [saying], \"Take what We have given you with determination and listen.\" They said [instead], \"We hear and disobey.\" And their hearts absorbed [the worship of] the calf because of their disbelief. Say, \"How wretched is that which your faith enjoins upon you, if you should be believers.\" [Al-Baqara: 93]\nThe Holy Quran gives these calf-worshippers the news about a terrible punishment both in this world and in the Hereafter:\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ سَيَنَالُهُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِمْ وَذِلَّةٌ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا ۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُفْتَرِينَ\nIndeed, those who took the calf [for worship] will obtain anger from their Lord and humiliation in the life of this world, and thus do We recompense the inventors [of falsehood].\n[Al-A’raf: 152]\nWe come to know from the history of the Jews, that they could never free themselves of this calf-worship. When the kingdom of Bani-Israel was divided into two parts, Yarbaam-bin-Naabaat, the king of the northern part had two idols of the calf made. He placed one in ‘Eel’ and the other in ‘Daan’. Then the Bani-Israel started making idols of the bull also and started keeping them in their prayer-houses due to which the worship of the calf and the bull was very popular. The Bible describes this in many places."],[77,"§Caliph\nThe meaning of Khalifa is ‘representative’ or a person who comes after another. That is why Abu Bakr(ra) is called Khalifa (administrator or representative) because he became the ruler of Muslims after the Holy Prophet(saws). After him Umar(ra) became the ruler and the system of caliphs went on.\nThe Holy Quran says about the selection of caliphs:\nيَا دَاوُودُ إِنَّا جَعَلْنَاكَ خَلِيفَةً فِي الْأَرْضِ فَاحْكُم بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعِ الْهَوَىٰ فَيُضِلَّكَ عَن سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ\n[We said], \"O David, indeed We have made you a successor upon the earth, so judge between the people in truth and do not follow [your own] desire, as it will lead you astray from the way of Allah.\"\n[Saad: 26]\nDawood(as) has been called a caliph because he was made the king in the place of ‘Shawal’. We understand from this that even a king can be called a caliph. Allah(swt) made Adam(as) and his descendants, namely mankind the caliphs:\nوَإِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ إِنِّي جَاعِلٌ فِي الْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً ۖ قَالُوا أَتَجْعَلُ فِيهَا مَن يُفْسِدُ فِيهَا وَيَسْفِكُ الدِّمَاءَ وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ ۖ قَالَ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ\nBehold, thy Lord said to the angels: \"I will create a vicegerent on earth.\" They said: \"Wilt Thou place therein one who will make mischief therein and shed blood? - whilst we do celebrate Thy praises and glorify Thy holy (name)?\" He said: \"I know what ye know not.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 30]\nوَهُوَ الَّذِي جَعَلَكُمْ خَلَائِفَ الْأَرْضِ وَرَفَعَ بَعْضَكُمْ فَوْقَ بَعْضٍ دَرَجَاتٍ لِّيَبْلُوَكُمْ فِي مَا آتَاكُمْ ۗ\nIt is He Who hath made you (His) agents, inheritors of the earth: He hath raised you in ranks, some above others: that He may try you in the gifts He hath given you.\n[Al-An’aam: 165]\nWho were present on earth before Adam(as) and his descendants in whose place man was being made the caliph? One school of thought says that they were the jinn, and the angels seeing their deeds said that they would create mischief. Or it may be possible that Allah(swt) said that he was going to make such a creature the caliph on earth who had the power to think and understand and would have the freedom to act according to his will. The angels then said that in that case there would be mischief on earth.\nIn the same way after the flood of Nuh(as), the tribe of Hud was made the caliphs:\nوَاذْكُرُوا إِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَاءَ مِن بَعْدِ قَوْمِ نُوحٍ وَزَادَكُمْ فِي الْخَلْقِ بَسْطَةً ۖ\nCall in remembrance that He made you inheritors after the people of Noah, and gave you a stature tall among the nations.\n[Al-A’raaf: 69]\nSimilarly after the tribe of ‘Aad’, the tribe of ‘Thamud’ were made the caliphs:\nوَاذْكُرُوا إِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَاءَ مِن بَعْدِ عَادٍ وَبَوَّأَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ\nAnd remember how He made you inheritors after the 'Ad people and gave you habitations in the land.\n[Al-A’raaf: 74]\nIn these verses, the meaning of ‘Khalifa’ is one tribe inhabiting the land in place of another. The word is used in the same sense in another place:\nثُمَّ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ خَلَائِفَ فِي الْأَرْضِ مِن بَعْدِهِمْ لِنَنظُرَ كَيْفَ تَعْمَلُونَ\nThen We made you heirs in the land after them, to see how ye would behave!\n[Yunus: 14]\nThat is why haakim(administrator) is also called a caliph because he is appointed in place of his predecessor. And this meaning was preferred among the ‘Salph’ (ancient Islamic scholars).Ibn-Jareer has given another meaning to caliph which is ‘a person sent to earth to implement the commands of Allah(swt)’. That is, first Adam(as) and then the ummah of Muhammad(saws) were made the caliphs. But the first meaning appears to be correct because if the second meaning had been correct then there was no cause for apprehension on the part of the angels."],[78,"§Camel\nIn the Holy Quran, three words are used for camel:\nJamal\nNaakha\nIbeel\nJamal: This is used in the masculine gender:\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا بِآيَاتِنَا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوا عَنْهَا لَا تُفَتَّحُ لَهُمْ أَبْوَابُ السَّمَاءِ وَلَا يَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ حَتَّىٰ يَلِجَ الْجَمَلُ فِي سَمِّ الْخِيَاطِ ۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُجْرِمِينَ\nTo those who reject Our signs and treat them with arrogance, no opening will there be of the gates of heaven, nor will they enter the garden, until the camel can pass through the eye of the needle: Such is Our reward for those in sin.\n[Al-A’raaf: 40]\nThat is, the disbelievers are being warned here that until and unless they believe in the Almighty Allah(swt) and His book the Holy Quran, they cannot even dream of entering paradise just as the camel cannot enter through the eye of the needle.\nNaakha: This is used in the feminine gender. It means a she-camel. This word occurs seven times in the Holy Quran but in the context of one incident related to the tribe of Saleh(as). Allah(swt) sent a she-camel as a sign from Him with Saleh(as). Saleh(as) addressed the people of his tribe as:\nوَإِلَىٰ ثَمُودَ أَخَاهُمْ صَالِحًا ۗ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ ۖ قَدْ جَاءَتْكُم بَيِّنَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ ۖ هَٰذِهِ نَاقَةُ اللَّهِ لَكُمْ آيَةً ۖ فَذَرُوهَا تَأْكُلْ فِي أَرْضِ اللَّهِ ۖ وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوءٍ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ\nTo the Thamud people (We sent) Salih, one of their own brethren: He said: \"O my people! worship Allah: ye have no other god but Him. Now hath come unto you a clear (Sign) from your Lord! This she-camel of Allah is a Sign unto you: So leave her to graze in Allah's earth, and let her come to no harm, or ye shall be seized with a grievous punishment.\n[Al-A’raaf: 73]\n﴿قَالَ هَٰذِهِ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُومٍ ١٥٥ وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوءٍ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ١٥٦ فَعَقَرُوهَا فَأَصْبَحُوا نَادِمِينَ ١٥٧﴾\nHe said: \"Here is a she-camel: she has a right of watering, and ye have a right of watering, (severally) on a day appointed. \"Touch her not with harm, lest the Penalty of a Great Day seize you.\" But they ham-strung her: then did they become full of regrets.\n[Ash-Shu’aara: 155-157]\nوَمَا مَنَعَنَا أَن نُّرْسِلَ بِالْآيَاتِ إِلَّا أَن كَذَّبَ بِهَا الْأَوَّلُونَ ۚ وَآتَيْنَا ثَمُودَ النَّاقَةَ مُبْصِرَةً فَظَلَمُوا بِهَا ۚ وَمَا نُرْسِلُ بِالْآيَاتِ إِلَّا تَخْوِيفًا\nAnd We refrain from sending the signs, only because the men of former generations treated them as false: We sent the she-camel to the Thamud to open their eyes, but they treated her wrongfully: We only send the Signs by way of terror (and warning from evil).\n[Bani-Israel: 59]\n﴿وَيَا قَوْمِ هَٰذِهِ نَاقَةُ اللَّهِ لَكُمْ آيَةً فَذَرُوهَا تَأْكُلْ فِي أَرْضِ اللَّهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوءٍ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ قَرِيبٌ ٦٤ فَعَقَرُوهَا فَقَالَ تَمَتَّعُوا فِي دَارِكُمْ ثَلَاثَةَ أَيَّامٍ ۖ ذَٰلِكَ وَعْدٌ غَيْرُ مَكْذُوبٍ ٦٥ فَلَمَّا جَاءَ أَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا صَالِحًا وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَعَهُ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَمِنْ خِزْيِ يَوْمِئِذٍ ۗ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْقَوِيُّ الْعَزِيزُ ٦٦﴾\n\"And O my people! This she-camel of Allah is a symbol to you: leave her to feed on Allah's (free) earth, and inflict no harm on her, or a swift penalty will seize you!\" But they did ham-string her. So he said: \"Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days: (Then will be your ruin): (Behold) there a promise not to be belied!\" When Our Decree issued, We saved Salih and those who believed with him, by (special) Grace from Ourselves - and from the Ignominy of that day. For thy Lord - He is the Strong One, and able to enforce His Will.\n[Hud: 64-66]\n﴿فَقَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ نَاقَةَ اللَّهِ وَسُقْيَاهَا ١٣ فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَعَقَرُوهَا فَدَمْدَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ رَبُّهُم بِذَنبِهِمْ فَسَوَّاهَا ١٤ وَلَا يَخَافُ عُقْبَاهَا ١٥﴾\nBut the Messenger of Allah said to them: \"It is a She-camel of Allah! And (bar her not from) having her drink!\" Then they rejected him (as a false prophet), and they hamstrung her. So their Lord, on account of their crime, obliterated their traces and made them equal (in destruction, high and low)! And for Him is no fear of its consequences.\n[Ash-Shams: 13-15]\nSo, this was the fate of the tribe of Saleh(as), Thamud who not only rejected the sign which was a she-camel but also killed her. Then, they were seized in a terrible punishment from Allah(swt). Not only does the Holy Quran confirm the previously revealed divine books, but also criticises and forbids the changes and additions which the people had done to them; for example the Jews had added to the Taurah on their own that Allah(swt) regrets his actions which is obviously utterly false. (Genesis: 6:4-6, 8:12)\nWhatever Allah(swt) does, He(swt) does it in His infinite mercy and wisdom and there cannot be any possibility of regret or fear on His part.\nIbeel: This word is used in both the masculine and feminine gender. This word occurs in two places in the Holy Quran:\nIn the surah Al-An’aam where the beasts of burden have been described and in the same way the animals whose meat is halal.\n(See: Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’aam, Verses-143-145)\nIn the surah Al-Ghashiyah, the earth, the skies and many other things which Allah(swt) has created have been described and the camel is one of them. When man gives a little thought to this vast, systematic and beautiful creation, believing in the Day of Judgement will not be difficult at all.\n(See: Quran, Surah-88, Al-Ghashiyah, Verse-17)"],[79,"§Children\nIt is through one’s children or progeny or offspring that the lineage of a tribe continues; be it in case of humans or other creatures. So, it is one of the greatest gifts of Allah(swt). The Holy Quran says:\n﴿لِّلَّهِ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۚ يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَاءُ ۚ يَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ إِنَاثًا وَيَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ الذُّكُورَ ٤٩ أَوْ يُزَوِّجُهُمْ ذُكْرَانًا وَإِنَاثًا ۖ وَيَجْعَلُ مَن يَشَاءُ عَقِيمًا ۚ إِنَّهُ عَلِيمٌ قَدِيرٌ ٥٠﴾\nTo Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth; He creates what he wills. He gives to whom He wills female [children], and He gives to whom He wills males. Or He makes them [both] males and females, and He renders whom He wills barren. Indeed, He is Knowing and Competent.\n[Ash-Shura: 49, 50]\nThe birth and death of all creatures is at the explicit command of Allah(swt). No one can interfere in this. The above verse is for the people who go to saints, god-men, graves etc. to fulfill their wish for a child of their own. These people are actually men like them and have no power to grant their wishes. The foolish people make these people partners of Allah(swt) and seek their blessings when in all matters absolutely no one can interfere in the Sovereignty of Allah(swt).\nWe must bear in mind that when the doctors, hakims, physicians etc, treat the patients, it is not against the above verse because according to a sahih hadith:\n“Allah(swt) has created a cure for every disease.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5678)\nSo, the medicines are only effective if Allah(swt) wishes it. We do come across cases where the same medicine is effective in the case of one patient while it is completely useless in someone else’s case.\nIn the same way, even the modern methods of conception depend on the will of Allah(swt) only. If He(swt) does not wish so, nothing can happen. He(swt) may give sons to some, daughters to some, or both to some and some women may be destined to remain barren. So, all of us must keep praying to Allah(swt) as:\nO Allah(swt)! You are the Greatest, Your Greatness is unlimited. We exalt You alone and worship You alone and to You alone do we turn for help."],[80,"§Cow\nThe cow is called ‘Baqara’ in Arabic. It is found in most of the places in the world. This has been used as a sacrificial animal since the ancient times. During the time of Musa(as) also cows were being sacrificed. But in the Bible it has been forbidden to sacrifice both the cow and its calf on the same day. (See Bible, Leviticus, 22:27)\nIn the Holy Quran, the cow has been described in four places:\nMusa(as) asking his tribe to sacrifice a cow. (See Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verses-67-71)\nThe description of the fat of cow being forbidden for the Jews. (See Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-146)\nThe explanation given by Yusuf(as) of the dream of the king of that land in which he sees seven fat cows being eaten by seven lean cows. (See Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verses-43-49)\nCow being mentioned as one of the sacrificial animals (See Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-144)"],[81,"§Creatures\nIn the Holy Quran, other than humans, jinn and the angels four types of creatures are described at various places. They are:\nAnimals: Elephant, horse, pig, camel, donkey, mule, monkey, dog, goat, cow, lion, wolf and calf.\nInsects, worms and crawling creatures: Ant, worm, spider etc.\nBirds and flying creatures: Crow, Hud-hud, honey-bee, house-fly, mosquito, locusts etc.\nCreatures living in water: Fish, frog etc."],[82,"§Crow\nCrow is a type of bird which is considered unclean because it eats impure and dirty things too. It is forbidden to eat the meat of the crow but at one time this small bird was a means of instruction for mankind.\nThe story is as follows: Adam(as) had two sons Cain and Abel. Both offered a sacrifice to Allah(swt). The sacrifice of Abel was accepted by Allah(swt) while that of Cain was not. This infuriated Cain who killed his brother. After that he did not know how to dispose of the body. Then, Allah(swt) sent down a crow to instruct him by example. This is described in the Holy Quran as:\nفَبَعَثَ اللَّهُ غُرَابًا يَبْحَثُ فِي الْأَرْضِ لِيُرِيَهُ كَيْفَ يُوَارِي سَوْءَةَ أَخِيهِ ۚ قَالَ يَا وَيْلَتَا أَعَجَزْتُ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِثْلَ هَٰذَا الْغُرَابِ فَأُوَارِيَ سَوْءَةَ أَخِي ۖ فَأَصْبَحَ مِنَ النَّادِمِينَ\nThen Allah sent a raven, who scratched the ground, to show him how to hide the shame of his brother. \"Woe is me!\" said he; \"Was I not even able to be as this raven, and to hide the shame of my brother?\" then he became full of regrets.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 31]\nThe killing of Abel is described even in the Taurah but not in as much detail as in the Holy Quran. There is just a reference to it in the Taurah:\nWhile they were in the field, Cain attacked his brother Abel and killed him.\nThen the Lord said to Cain, “Where is your brother Abel?”\n“I don’t know,” he replied. “Am I my brother’s keeper?”\nThe Lord said, “What have you done? Listen! Your brother’s blood cries out to me from the ground.\n(Genesis, 4:10)\nIt is being hinted here that he buried his brother in the earth. Since then the custom of burying the dead started so that man who was created from mud goes back into it and then be raised up from it on the Day of Resurrection."],[83,"§Daabba\n‘Daabba’ is described again and again in the Holy Quran. It can be translated as ‘creatures’. These also contain the hidden signs of Allah(swt):\nوَمِنْ آيَاتِهِ خَلْقُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَثَّ فِيهِمَا مِن دَابَّةٍ ۚ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ جَمْعِهِمْ إِذَا يَشَاءُ قَدِيرٌ\nAnd of his signs is the creation of the heavens and earth and what He has dispersed throughout them of creatures. And He, for gathering them when He wills, is competent.\n[Ash-Shura: 29]\nWe come to know from the above verse that life forms can be found even in the skies about which the scientists are trying to find out.\nDaabba being dispersed on the earth:\nوَمَا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مِن مَّاءٍ فَأَحْيَا بِهِ الْأَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا وَبَثَّ فِيهَا مِن كُلِّ دَابَّةٍ\nAllah has sent down from the heavens of rain, giving life thereby to the earth after its lifelessness and dispersing therein every [kind of] moving creature.\n[Al-Baqara: 164]\nDaabba prostrating before Allah(swt):\n﴿وَلِلَّهِ يَسْجُدُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ مِن دَابَّةٍ وَالْمَلَائِكَةُ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ ٤٩ يَخَافُونَ رَبَّهُم مِّن فَوْقِهِمْ وَيَفْعَلُونَ مَا يُؤْمَرُونَ ۩ ٥٠﴾\nAnd to Allah prostrates whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth of creatures, and the angels [as well], and they are not arrogant. They fear their Lord above them, and they do what they are commanded.\n[An-Nahl: 49, 50]\nProstrating before Allah(swt) and worshipping Him(swt) is the primary duty of every creature. The other creatures may not prostrate like the humans. It is also a fact that every creature fears Allah(swt). But the way in which the other creatures fear Allah(swt) is different from the way the humans do. Our knowledge is limited and it shall always remain so. It is impossible to even imagine the unlimited knowledge of Allah(swt). So, we should believe in the things which have been mentioned in the Holy Quran by Allah(swt) just as we believe in something which we see in front of our eyes.\nDaabba living in communities or groups:\nThe Holy Quran says:\nوَمَا مِن دَابَّةٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَا طَائِرٍ يَطِيرُ بِجَنَاحَيْهِ إِلَّا أُمَمٌ أَمْثَالُكُم ۚ مَّا فَرَّطْنَا فِي الْكِتَابِ مِن شَيْءٍ ۚ ثُمَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ يُحْشَرُونَ\nAnd there is no creature on [or within] the earth or bird that flies with its wings except [that they are] communities like you. We have not neglected in the Register a thing. Then unto their Lord they will be gathered.\n[Al-An’am: 38]\nThat is, no creature is alone either on the earth or in the skies; but live in communities or groups. Just as the destiny of every human being is written in the divine book ‘Lauhe-Mahfooz’, the destiny of every creature is also written in it and everyone gets its livelihood according to it. Then once its life-term gets over, it dies. All this has been recorded by Allah(swt) in the ‘Lauhe-Mahfooz.’\nLivelihood:\nThe Holy Quran says:\nوَمَا مِن دَابَّةٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ إِلَّا عَلَى اللَّهِ رِزْقُهَا وَيَعْلَمُ مُسْتَقَرَّهَا وَمُسْتَوْدَعَهَا ۚ كُلٌّ فِي كِتَابٍ مُّبِينٍ\nAnd there is no creature on earth but that upon Allah is its provision, and He knows its place of dwelling and place of storage. All is in a clear register.\n[Hud: 6]\nBy ‘place of storage’ is meant the place of its death.\nFor understanding the meaning of this verse, it is important to study the sahih hadith which says that Allah(swt) wrote the destiny of all creatures fifty thousand years before creating the earth and the skies. At that time the throne (Arsh) of Allah(swt) was on water. (Sahih Muslim, 2653)\nAllah(swt) deferring the punishment of the sinners:\nوَلَوْ يُؤَاخِذُ اللَّهُ النَّاسَ بِظُلْمِهِم مَّا تَرَكَ عَلَيْهَا مِن دَابَّةٍ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَخِّرُهُمْ إِلَىٰ أَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى ۖ فَإِذَا جَاءَ أَجَلُهُمْ لَا يَسْتَأْخِرُونَ سَاعَةً ۖ وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ\nAnd if Allah were to impose blame on the people for their wrongdoing, He would not have left upon the earth any creature, but He defers them for a specified term. And when their term has come, they will not remain behind an hour, nor will they precede [it].\n[An-Nahl: 61]\nThe Daabba coming out of the earth before the Last Day:\nOne of the signs of the Last Day is that a creature will come out of the earth which will speak to humans:\nوَإِذَا وَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ أَخْرَجْنَا لَهُمْ دَابَّةً مِّنَ الْأَرْضِ تُكَلِّمُهُمْ أَنَّ النَّاسَ كَانُوا بِآيَاتِنَا لَا يُوقِنُونَ\nAnd when the word befalls them, We will bring forth for them a creature from the earth speaking to them, [saying] that the people were, of Our verses, not certain [in faith].\n[An-Naml: 82]\nThis creature will tell humans that the teachings of the prophets were true but they rejected them. So, get ready for torment from Allah(swt). This Daabba preaching ‘Tawheed’ is actually an offense from Allah(swt) to the disbelievers that they did not listen to other humans (prophets), so now how can they reject this creature when believing will do them no good because the time for believing is past."],[84,"§Dawood(as)\nDawood(as) was a great prophet of Bani-Israel who has also been described in the Holy Quran. Most of the psalms of the Bible refer to him. According to the Bible, Dawood(as) was born around 1000 B.C. in Bethlehem in Palestine. His father was named ‘Passi’ who was from the tribe of Ibraheem(as). Allah(swt) made him very strong. One day while he was grazing his goats, a lion and a bear attacked him. Dawood(as) single-handedly killed both of them.(Bible, 1 Samuel 16/11, 17/34-36).\nThe Holy Quran also describes him as being very strong:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ مِنَّا فَضْلًا ۖ يَا جِبَالُ أَوِّبِي مَعَهُ وَالطَّيْرَ ۖ وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ الْحَدِيدَ ١٠ أَنِ اعْمَلْ سَابِغَاتٍ وَقَدِّرْ فِي السَّرْدِ ۖ وَاعْمَلُوا صَالِحًا ۖ إِنِّي بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ ١١﴾\nAnd We certainly gave David from Us bounty. [We said], \"O mountains, repeat [Our] praises with him, and the birds [as well].\" And We made pliable for him iron, [Commanding him], \"Make full coats of mail and calculate [precisely] the links, and work [all of you] righteousness. Indeed I, of what you do, am Seeing.\"\n[Saba: 10, 11]\nAt one place, the Holy Prophet(saws) is being advised to have patience and courage like Dawood(as), because even though Dawood(as) was strong and powerful, he did have to face difficulties. But he never left the path of Allah(swt):\nاصْبِرْ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَاذْكُرْ عَبْدَنَا دَاوُودَ ذَا الْأَيْدِ ۖ إِنَّهُ أَوَّابٌ\nBe patient over what they say and remember Our servant, David, the possessor of strength; indeed, he was one who repeatedly turned back [to Allah].\n[Sad: 17]\nAs a result, Allah(swt) made Dawood(as) the king:\nيَا دَاوُودُ إِنَّا جَعَلْنَاكَ خَلِيفَةً فِي الْأَرْضِ فَاحْكُم بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعِ الْهَوَىٰ فَيُضِلَّكَ عَن سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ\n[We said], \"O David, indeed We have made you a successor upon the earth, so judge between the people in truth and do not follow [your own] desire, as it will lead you astray from the way of Allah.\"\n[Sad: 26]\nThen upon the insistence of the Bani-Israel, Allah(swt) made a person named ‘Talut’ (Saul) their ruler to protect them from ‘Jalut’ (Goliath) who was attacking them continuously. Referring to this the Holy Quran says:\nأَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الْمَلَإِ مِن بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ مِن بَعْدِ مُوسَىٰ إِذْ قَالُوا لِنَبِيٍّ لَّهُمُ ابْعَثْ لَنَا مَلِكًا نُّقَاتِلْ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۖ\nHave you not considered the assembly of the Children of Israel after [the time of] Moses when they said to a prophet of theirs, \"Send to us a king, and we will fight in the way of Allah\"?\n[Al-Baqara: 246]\nوَقَالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ بَعَثَ لَكُمْ طَالُوتَ مَلِكًا ۚ\nAnd their prophet said to them, \"Indeed, Allah has sent to you Saul as a king.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 247]\nفَهَزَمُوهُم بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَقَتَلَ دَاوُودُ جَالُوتَ وَآتَاهُ اللَّهُ الْمُلْكَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَهُ مِمَّا يَشَاءُ ۗ\nSo they defeated them by permission of Allah, and David killed Goliath, and Allah gave him the kingship and prophethood and taught him from that which He willed.\n[Al-Baqara: 251]\nThis is described in the Bible as follows:\nJalut or Goliath was a very wicked person and had attacked the Bani-Israel many times. He had also snatched away their ‘tabut’( a chest containing the relics left by the prophets Musa and Haroon(as)) which they had brought with them from Egypt. So, they requested their prophet Samuel to appoint a king for them so that under his leadership they could fight against the Philistines and the neighbouring kings. Their prophet appointed Shabul (who is called Talut in the Holy Quran) as their king. He went with his army to fight ‘Jalut’ and the armies came together at a place about fifteen miles from Bethlehem. Two of the sons of Dawood(as)’s father Passi were taking part in the fight. So, Passi sent Dawood(as) to get information about his brothers. When Dawood(as) reached there he saw that Jalut was challenging the soldiers of Talut but fearing his massive build no one dared to take up the challenge. Dawood(as) could not bear it. He took careful aim and hit Goliath with three stones upon which blood started flowing from his forehead and he fell down. Dawood(as) walked up to him and using his sword killed him. This took place around 1010 B.C. When Talut came to know about this he was very happy and got his daughter married to Dawood(as) and made him the general of his army. The Bani-Israel were very impressed with Dawood(as) and started singing his praises. This made Talut very jealous and he started plotting to kill Dawood(as). So, Dawood(as) ran away to Habroon where he was made the king by the people there. He ruled there for seven and a half years. After the death of Talut, the Bani-Israel made him their king. He died in 971 B.C. He was succeeded by his son Sulaiman(as).\nDawood(as) was not only a great ruler but also a great prophet who was sent for the guidance of the Bani-Israel. He was given the divine book ‘Zabur’. The Holy Quran says:\nوَآتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ زَبُورًا\nto David We gave the book [of Psalms].\n[An-Nisa: 163] [Bani-Israel: 55]\nHe would recite the Zabur in such a melodious voice that the birds and mountains would join him in exalting Allah(swt):\nوَسَخَّرْنَا مَعَ دَاوُودَ الْجِبَالَ يُسَبِّحْنَ وَالطَّيْرَ ۚ وَكُنَّا فَاعِلِينَ\nAnd We subjected the mountains to exalt [Us], along with David and [also] the birds. And We were doing [that].\n[Al-Anbiya: 79]\nوَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ مِنَّا فَضْلًا ۖ يَا جِبَالُ أَوِّبِي مَعَهُ وَالطَّيْرَ ۖ وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ الْحَدِيدَ\nAnd We certainly gave David from Us bounty. [We said], \"O mountains, repeat [Our] praises with him, and the birds [as well].\" And We made pliable for him iron.\n[Saba: 10]\n﴿إِنَّا سَخَّرْنَا الْجِبَالَ مَعَهُ يُسَبِّحْنَ بِالْعَشِيِّ وَالْإِشْرَاقِ ١٨ وَالطَّيْرَ مَحْشُورَةً ۖ كُلٌّ لَّهُ أَوَّابٌ ١٩﴾\nIndeed, We subjected the mountains [to praise] with him, exalting [Allah] in the [late] afternoon and [after] sunrise. And the birds were assembled, all with him repeating [praises].\n[Sad: 18, 19]\nThe melodious voice of Dawood(as) has been described in detail in the Bible. (1 Chronicles, 6:31, 16:7, 41-43, 25-1)\nAllah(swt) revealed the Zabur to Dawood(as) which was recited and memorized by people for many years. The fact is that the scholars found the Zabur in 5 B.C. At that time the Zabur was in the form of psalms. Then later on they found some more psalms. They combined these two to form a book which had 150 psalms. Of these 73 were composed by Dawood(as) and the remaining by others. This was then divided into five books. The first book contained 41 psalms, 37 credited to Dawood(as) and the rest to others. It is difficult to make sure as to who composed them; so they are called ‘orphan psalms’. The second book contains 31 psalms of which 18 are credited to Dawood(as) and the rest to others. The third book contains 17 psalms of which only one was composed by Dawood(as) and the remaining by others. The fourth book contains a total of 17 psalms of which only 2 were composed by Dawood(as) while the rest are by others. The fifth book contains 44 psalms of which 15 are credited to Dawood(as) and the rest to others.\n(See: Khamoos Kitab Muqaddas, p. 430, 431)\nThe Holy Quran gives a high position to Dawood(as). Allah(swt) made his kingdom very strong and made him so wise that he could solve the most complex problem with the greatest ease:\nوَشَدَدْنَا مُلْكَهُ وَآتَيْنَاهُ الْحِكْمَةَ وَفَصْلَ الْخِطَابِ\nAnd We strengthened his kingdom and gave him wisdom and discernment in speech.\n[Sad: 20]\nThe Holy Quran describes an incident which proves his wisdom. Two persons came up to him with a problem. One of them said:\nإِنَّ هَٰذَا أَخِي لَهُ تِسْعٌ وَتِسْعُونَ نَعْجَةً وَلِيَ نَعْجَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ فَقَالَ أَكْفِلْنِيهَا وَعَزَّنِي فِي الْخِطَابِ\nIndeed this, my brother, has ninety-nine ewes, and I have one ewe; so he said, 'Entrust her to me,' and he overpowered me in speech.\"\n[Sad: 23]\nDawood(as) declared this act of his brother’s wrong and gave a wise decision. Then he remembered some incident of his and fell down in prostration seeking the forgiveness of Allah(swt).\nAs to what this incident was, neither the Holy Quran nor the sahih hadith give an explanation. But it is possible that the ninety-nine goats described in verse-23 of surah Sad refer to his wives because in the Arabic language goats are compared to women.\nAbdullah ibn-Abbas has said that Dawood(as) asked the man (who is called Uriah the Hittite in the Bible) to get separated from his wife. This has been described in the commentary by Abdul-Muzaffar Samaani (died in 489 A.H).\nSo, when Dawood(as) came to know of his mistake, he fell down in prostration and sought the forgiveness of Allah(swt).\nSuch a small incident has been blown out of proportion in the Bible which says that Dawood(as) committed adultery with the wife of the Hittite and intentionally got him killed in a war and married his wife after his death.\nThe complete description is given in 2 Samuel 11-12.\nAmong the miracles which Allah(swt) had bestowed upon Dawood(as), one was that He(swt) made iron as soft as wax in his hands. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ الْحَدِيدَ ١٠ أَنِ اعْمَلْ سَابِغَاتٍ وَقَدِّرْ فِي السَّرْدِ ۖ﴾\nAnd We made pliable for him iron, [Commanding him], \"Make full coats of mail and calculate [precisely] the links.\n[Saba: 10-11]\nIn this way Allah(swt) bestowed many favours on Dawood(as) because he was a great devotee.\nإِنَّهُ أَوَّابٌ\nindeed, he was one who repeatedly turned back [to Allah].\n[Sad: 17]\nAllah(swt) advises patience to Prophet Muhammad(saws) by reciting the story of Dawood(as) that just as Dawood(as) was given the reward for his good deeds and the kingdom; the Holy Prophet shall also get his just reward."],[85,"§Days being interchanged\nIn this vast creation of Allah(swt), one of His systems is to keep interchanging the days and the state of the various tribes. At one point of time superiority is granted to one tribe and to some other tribe after a time. The Holy Quran says:\nإِن يَمْسَسْكُمْ قَرْحٌ فَقَدْ مَسَّ الْقَوْمَ قَرْحٌ مِّثْلُهُ ۚ وَتِلْكَ الْأَيَّامُ نُدَاوِلُهَا بَيْنَ النَّاسِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَيَتَّخِذَ مِنكُمْ شُهَدَاءَ ۗ وَاللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ\nIf a wound should touch you - there has already touched the [opposing] people a wound similar to it. And these days [of varying conditions] We alternate among the people so that Allah may make evident those who believe and [may] take to Himself from among you martyrs - and Allah does not like the wrongdoers.\n[Al-i-Imran: 140]\nIn the above verse, referring to the battles of Badr and Uhud, Allah(swt) explains one of his rules. It is that due to the interchanging of days, if the Muslims face some difficulty, then they should bear it with courage. If they are facing hard times at present, then they did have easy times before that. That is, everything is according to some master plan. Muslims should never be disheartened that Allah(swt) is granting success to the disbelievers and enemies of Islam because everything is according to a definite plan. If Allah(swt) forcibly converts everyone to Islam or if He(swt) grants success only to the Muslims, then there will not be any disbelievers left. This worldly life will not be a test anymore nor will the Day of Judgement have any meaning. But if Allah(swt) wishes He(swt) can make everybody a Muslim:\nوَلَوْ شَاءَ رَبُّكَ لَآمَنَ مَن فِي الْأَرْضِ كُلُّهُمْ جَمِيعًا ۚ أَفَأَنتَ تُكْرِهُ النَّاسَ حَتَّىٰ يَكُونُوا مُؤْمِنِينَ\nAnd had your Lord willed, those on earth would have believed - all of them entirely. Then, [O Muhammad], would you compel the people in order that they become believers?\n[Yunus: 99]\nThat is, when Allah(swt) Himself is not forcing people to become Muslims, then how can you O Muhammad(saws) force them to do so?\nThis is actually a warning to those people who were blaming the Holy Prophet(saws) that he was forcibly converting people to Islam at the point of the sword.\nAt one place Allah(swt) has also mentioned the words of the disbelievers:\nسَيَقُولُ الَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا لَوْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ مَا أَشْرَكْنَا وَلَا آبَاؤُنَا وَلَا حَرَّمْنَا مِن شَيْءٍ ۚ\nThose who associated with Allah will say, \"If Allah had willed, we would not have associated [anything] and neither would our fathers, nor would we have prohibited anything.\"\n[Al-An’am: 148]\nBut it is the rule of Allah(swt) that whatever someone desires, He(swt) lets him live in that state. He(swt) does not forcibly make someone follow Islam.\nSo, what the Muslims need to do when the times are adverse is to have patience, face them with courage and keep praying to the Almighty(swt) because without His will nothing can happen.\nAmong the most important teachings of the Holy Quran one is:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُغَيِّرُ مَا بِقَوْمٍ حَتَّىٰ يُغَيِّرُوا مَا بِأَنفُسِهِمْ ۗ\nIndeed, Allah will not change the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves.\n[Ar-Ra’d: 11]\nAddressing especially the Muslims, Allah(swt) is mentioning one of the common rules of His that their condition will not improve until and unless they themselves make an effort to improve it. Whether it is financial betterment, social upliftment or scientific development, we Muslims have to make an all-out effort and the help of Allah(swt) will InshaAllah follow."],[86,"§Dead Animals\nIt is forbidden to eat dead animals. But if forced by extreme hunger someone does so, then it is not a sin. (See Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-173)\nFor example, if there is absolutely nothing to eat and there is fear of death due to hunger, then dead animals can be eaten but not out of a desire to eat them. And only so much should be eaten as required."],[87,"§Dog\nDog is a dirty animal which freely roams around everywhere and even eats up dead animals. That is why eating its flesh has been forbidden in all the religious books.\nOn the other hand, a dog has certain qualities which are not found in any other animal. For instance, it is very faithful to its master. When the ‘people of the cave’ went to hide in the cave, their dog was also with them as is described in the Holy Quran:\nوَتَحْسَبُهُمْ أَيْقَاظًا وَهُمْ رُقُودٌ ۚ وَنُقَلِّبُهُمْ ذَاتَ الْيَمِينِ وَذَاتَ الشِّمَالِ ۖ وَكَلْبُهُم بَاسِطٌ ذِرَاعَيْهِ بِالْوَصِيدِ ۚ\nThou wouldst have deemed them awake, whilst they were asleep, and We turned them on their right and on their left sides: their dog stretching forth his two fore-legs on the threshold.\n[Al-Kahf: 18]\nWhen there was a dispute concerning the exact number of people in the cave, the people started saying:\nسَيَقُولُونَ ثَلَاثَةٌ رَّابِعُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ وَيَقُولُونَ خَمْسَةٌ سَادِسُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ رَجْمًا بِالْغَيْبِ ۖ وَيَقُولُونَ سَبْعَةٌ وَثَامِنُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ ۚ\n(Some) say they were three, the dog being the fourth among them; (others) say they were five, the dog being the sixth,- doubtfully guessing at the unknown; (yet others) say they were seven, the dog being the eighth.\n[Al-Kahf: 22]\nIt is due to this quality of the dog that it is allowed to keep it under two conditions:\nFor hunting purposes:\nIf it has been trained to hunt; that is bring the game to its master. The Holy Quran says:\nيَسْأَلُونَكَ مَاذَا أُحِلَّ لَهُمْ ۖ قُلْ أُحِلَّ لَكُمُ الطَّيِّبَاتُ ۙ وَمَا عَلَّمْتُم مِّنَ الْجَوَارِحِ مُكَلِّبِينَ تُعَلِّمُونَهُنَّ مِمَّا عَلَّمَكُمُ اللَّهُ ۖ فَكُلُوا مِمَّا أَمْسَكْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَاذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ ۖ\nThey ask thee what is lawful to them (as food). Say: lawful unto you are (all) things good and pure: and what ye have taught your trained hunting animals (to catch) in the manner directed to you by Allah: eat what they catch for you, but pronounce the name of Allah over it.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 4]\nThe scholars are of the opinion that a dog can be considered as an animal which is trained to hunt. Training it to hunt means that when it is freed to hunt it chases the game and when called back it comes back to its master. The game hunted by such an animal is halal under two conditions.\nFirst that when the animal is freed, the name of Allah(swt) is pronounced. Second the prey is brought back to the master and the hunting animal has not begun to eat it. Even if the prey is dead, eating it is halal as the rules are the same as in the case of ‘Zabiha’.\nAccording to a sahih hadith of Adi-bin-Haatim:\n“If you leave the hunting dog to hunt taking the name of Allah(swt), eat the game which it has caught even if it is dead. But if the dog has eaten some of it, then do not eat it because I suspect that it has hunted it for itself. In the same way if it has hunted along with another dog, then do not eat it.”\n(Bukhari, 5483 and Muslim, 1929)\nTo use the dog to safeguard the domestic animals:\n“If somebody keeps a dog other than for hunting or safeguarding the domestic animals; then from his account of good deeds everyday there will be a reduction of two ‘qiraat’.”\n(Bukhari, 5480 and Muslim, 1574)\n(Qiraat is a unit of weight which is equivalent to the weight of three wheat grains of gold)\nIn another hadith it says:\n“And for safeguarding the fields.” (Sahih Muslim)\nA dog may also be kept for safeguarding the house provided it does not enter the house.\nOne bad habit of the dog to which the Holy Quran refers to is its greed and gluttony. It is always sniffing the earth in search of something to eat. One other bad habit is that whether you give it something to eat or not, it is always lolling out its tongue. The example of a dog is given with respect to a person who has been given knowledge, wealth and respect in this world by Allah(swt). Such a man should ideally have recognized and embraced the truth, but his wealth and power made him so arrogant that he was ungrateful to Allah(swt) and became a disbeliever. Such a person is like the dog who lolls out its tongue whether or not you give it anything :\n﴿وَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَأَ الَّذِي آتَيْنَاهُ آيَاتِنَا فَانسَلَخَ مِنْهَا فَأَتْبَعَهُ الشَّيْطَانُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْغَاوِينَ ١٧٥ وَلَوْ شِئْنَا لَرَفَعْنَاهُ بِهَا وَلَٰكِنَّهُ أَخْلَدَ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ وَاتَّبَعَ هَوَاهُ ۚ فَمَثَلُهُ كَمَثَلِ الْكَلْبِ إِن تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْهِ يَلْهَثْ أَوْ تَتْرُكْهُ يَلْهَث ۚ ذَّٰلِكَ مَثَلُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا بِآيَاتِنَا ۚ فَاقْصُصِ الْقَصَصَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ١٧٦﴾\nRelate to them the story of the man to whom We sent Our signs, but he passed them by: so Satan followed him up, and he went astray. If it had been Our will, We should have elevated him with Our signs; but he inclined to the earth, and followed his own vain desires. His similitude is that of a dog: if you attack him, he lolls out his tongue, or if you leave him alone, he (still) lolls out his tongue. That is the similitude of those who reject Our signs; So relate the story; perchance they may reflect.\n[Al-A’raaf: 175-176]\nIf the dogs become a menace to the society, then they can be killed because a dog-bite may cause rabies which can prove fatal. All these rules which are a part and parcel of Islam are for the benefit and safety of mankind as has been proved time and again."],[88,"§Donkey\nA donkey is a domestic animal. It has two special qualities:\nOne is that how much ever load you put on it, it will bear it patiently.\nThe second is that it is a very dumb creature. That is why people with very low intelligence are compared to it. Donkeys are of two kinds:\nThe wild donkey: This is called ‘Wahshi’ in Arabic. Its flesh is halal.\nThe domestic donkey: This is called ‘Himar’. Its flesh is forbidden.\nFrom ancient times, a donkey has been used for various tasks. From Ibraheem(as) to the Last Prophet(saws), all the prophets have used it for riding and even today it is used in various places for travel.\nIbraheem(as) rode a donkey. (see Bible, Genesis, 22:3)\nYaqub(as) owned many donkeys. (See Bible, Genesis, 30:43)\nIsa(as) entered Jerusalem riding his donkey. (See Bible, Matthew, 21:5,7)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) also used a donkey for travelling. The donkey’s name was ‘Ufair’. Another donkey which the Holy Prophet(saws) used was named ‘Yafur’ which was presented to him by Farwa-bin-Amr Juzami. The Holy Quran describes the donkey as a beast for riding:\nوَالْخَيْلَ وَالْبِغَالَ وَالْحَمِيرَ لِتَرْكَبُوهَا وَزِينَةً ۚ وَيَخْلُقُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ\nAnd [He created] the horses, mules and donkeys for you to ride and [as] adornment. And He creates that which you do not know.\n[An-Nahl: 8]\nThe other contexts in which the donkey is mentioned:\n1. The people who had been given the Taurah but did not follow it have been compared to the donkeys:\nمَثَلُ الَّذِينَ حُمِّلُوا التَّوْرَاةَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَحْمِلُوهَا كَمَثَلِ الْحِمَارِ يَحْمِلُ أَسْفَارًا ۚ بِئْسَ مَثَلُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا بِآيَاتِ اللَّهِ ۚ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ\nThe example of those who were entrusted with the Torah and then did not take it on is like that of a donkey who carries volumes [of books]. Wretched is the example of the people who deny the signs of Allah. And Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.\n[Al-Jumu’a: 5]\n2. The voice of the donkey has been described as the most unpleasant voice:\nوَاقْصِدْ فِي مَشْيِكَ وَاغْضُضْ مِن صَوْتِكَ ۚ إِنَّ أَنكَرَ الْأَصْوَاتِ لَصَوْتُ الْحَمِيرِ\nAnd be moderate in your pace and lower your voice; indeed, the most disagreeable of sounds is the voice of donkeys.\"\n[Luqman: 19]\nWhen the wrong-doers are advised good things they become restless like the donkey does when he sees the lion:\n﴿فَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِينَ ٤٩ كَأَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٌ مُّسْتَنفِرَةٌ ٥٠ فَرَّتْ مِن قَسْوَرَةٍ ٥١﴾\nThen what is [the matter] with them that they are, from the reminder, turning away. As if they were alarmed donkeys. Fleeing from a lion?\n[Al-Muddathir: 49-51]"],[89,"§Dried Ginger\n(See Zanzabeel)"],[90,"§Duwa(Supplication)\nDuwa or supplication is a form of worship because through the supplications the slave presents himself in a very humble way before Allah(swt). And moreover he begs Allah(swt) fully convinced that Allah(swt) alone is the One who can give him whatever he desires and hence the slave has to ask from Allah(swt) alone. Allah(swt) Himself commands in the Holy Quran to ask Him(swt) alone for anything and He(swt) shall give:\nوَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ادْعُونِي أَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِي سَيَدْخُلُونَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ\nAnd your Lord says, \"Call upon Me; I will respond to you.\" Indeed, those who disdain My worship will enter Hell [rendered] contemptible.\n[Al-Momin: 60]\nادْعُوا رَبَّكُمْ تَضَرُّعًا وَخُفْيَةً ۚ إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِينَ\nCall upon your Lord in humility and privately; indeed, He does not like transgressors.\n[Al-A’raf: 55]\nThat is, supplication or duwa is actually worshipping Allah(swt) as is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“Supplication is worship.”\n(Abu Dawood, 1479; Tirmizi, 2969; Ibn-Maaja, 3828 and Musnad Ahmad 8:267)\nIt is compulsory for every Muslim to supplicate to Allah(swt) because supplication can change one’s destiny as is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“Nothing can change destiny except duwa or supplication.”\n(Tirmizi, 2139; Ibn-Maaja, 4022; Musnad Ahmad, 5:277)\nBut destiny which is already written cannot be undone; so the meaning of this hadith is that the duwa which does not clash with destiny will be accepted. As we have no knowledge about our destiny we should keep asking Allah(swt) that our prayers are accepted without clashing with our destiny because supplication is itself a part of destiny.\nIt is for this reason that the prayer of the prophets was:\nوَأَيُّوبَ إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ أَنِّي مَسَّنِيَ الضُّرُّ وَأَنتَ أَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nAnd [mention] Job, when he called to his Lord, \"Indeed, adversity has touched me, and you are the Most Merciful of the merciful.\"\n[Al-Anbiya: 83]\nWhether the prayers are accepted or not, we do experience a sense of peace and get the courage to face the difficulties facing us. It is narrated in one sahih hadith:\nWhenever a Muslim supplicates to Allah(swt) with a supplication other than a sin or something which disconnects him from his family, Allah(swt) fulfills it in one of three ways: either Allah(swt) responds to his supplication quickly, or keeps his supplication until the day of Judgement, or wards off some evil. So the people said: “In that case we shall supplicate a lot.” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Allah(swt) gives more than that.” (See Musnad Ahmad, 11133)\nWe understand from above that supplication itself is worship and like other forms of worship it is for Allah(swt) alone. When somebody invokes someone other than Allah(swt), begs others for favours etc., then it becomes ‘shirk.’\nThe Holy Quran says:\nوَأَنَّ الْمَسَاجِدَ لِلَّهِ فَلَا تَدْعُوا مَعَ اللَّهِ أَحَدًا\nAnd [He revealed] that the masjids are for Allah, so do not invoke with Allah anyone.\n[Al-Jinn: 18]\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ عِبَادٌ أَمْثَالُكُمْ ۖ فَادْعُوهُمْ فَلْيَسْتَجِيبُوا لَكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ\nIndeed, those you [polytheists] call upon besides Allah are servants like you. So call upon them and let them respond to you, if you should be truthful.\n[Al-A’raf: 194]\nThe truth is:\nوَالَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِهِ لَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ نَصْرَكُمْ وَلَا أَنفُسَهُمْ يَنصُرُونَ\nAnd those you call upon besides Him are unable to help you, nor can they help themselves.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 197]\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِهِ مَا يَمْلِكُونَ مِن قِطْمِيرٍ ١٣ إِن تَدْعُوهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوا دُعَاءَكُمْ وَلَوْ سَمِعُوا مَا اسْتَجَابُوا لَكُمْ ۖ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ يَكْفُرُونَ بِشِرْكِكُمْ ۚ وَلَا يُنَبِّئُكَ مِثْلُ خَبِيرٍ ١٤﴾\nAnd those whom you invoke other than Him do not possess [as much as] the membrane of a date seed. If you invoke them, they do not hear your supplication; and if they heard, they would not respond to you. And on the Day of Resurrection they will deny your association. And none can inform you like [one] Acquainted [with all matters].\n[Fatir: 13, 14]\nProphet Ilyas(as) said to the people of his tribe:\n﴿وَإِنَّ إِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٢٣ إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ١٢٤ أَتَدْعُونَ بَعْلًا وَتَذَرُونَ أَحْسَنَ الْخَالِقِينَ ١٢٥﴾\nAnd indeed, Elias was from among the messengers, When he said to his people, \"Will you not fear Allah? Do you call upon Ba'l and leave the best of creators - Allah, your Lord and the Lord of your first forefathers?\"\n[As-Saffat: 123-126]\nIf this is the case then all our supplications should be for Allah(swt) alone. That is why the Holy Prophet(saws) has given various supplications for different times and conditions. For example supplication to repay a debt, supplication to get relief from some ailment, supplication before embarking on a journey, supplication to get rid of some difficulty etc. These supplications are mentioned in the books of hadith.\nTherefore it is compulsory for every Muslim to memorise these supplications and keep praying to Allah(swt) using them to fulfill their needs. We should keep hoping that our wishes are fulfilled. It will be a most shocking thing on the Day of Judgement for the people who had invoked others besides Allah(swt), when the ones who were invoked will say, “When did we ask you to invoke us other than Allah(swt). And when did we say that we shall fulfill your desires. We dissociate ourselves from you and your shirk. We ourselves pray to Allah(swt) for our success and salvation. What help can we give you?”"],[91,"§Earth\nThis land upon which we roam about freely is one of the most miraculous creations of Allah(swt) in which there are numerous lessons for the wise and discerning. The Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّ فِي خَلْقِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَاخْتِلَافِ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ لَآيَاتٍ لِّأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ\nIndeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day are signs for those of understanding.\n[Al-i-Imran: 190]\nThe earth and sky were joined together:\nأَوَلَمْ يَرَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَنَّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ كَانَتَا رَتْقًا فَفَتَقْنَاهُمَا ۖ وَجَعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَاءِ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ حَيٍّ ۖ أَفَلَا يُؤْمِنُونَ\nHave those who disbelieved not considered that the heavens and the earth were a joined entity, and We separated them and made from water every living thing? Then will they not believe?\n[Al-Anbiya: 30]\nWe understand from the above verse that the earth and the sky were joined together since ancient times. So, the Holy Quran addresses the disbelievers saying that have they not given a thought to this fact?\nBy the skies is meant the stars, planets etc. which as soon as they were separated started moving in their respective orbits.\nAllah(swt) created this whole universe in six days:\nاللَّهُ الَّذِي خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ ۖ\nIt is Allah who created the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them in six days; then He established Himself above the Throne.\n[As-Sajda: 4]\nLike the skies, the earth also has seven layers:\nاللَّهُ الَّذِي خَلَقَ سَبْعَ سَمَاوَاتٍ وَمِنَ الْأَرْضِ مِثْلَهُنَّ يَتَنَزَّلُ الْأَمْرُ بَيْنَهُنَّ لِتَعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ أَحَاطَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا\nIt is Allah who has created seven heavens and of the earth, the like of them. [His] command descends among them so you may know that Allah is over all things competent and that Allah has encompassed all things in knowledge.\n[At-Talaq: 12]\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Whoever usurps even one span of the land of somebody, his neck will be encircled with it down the seven earths.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 1610)\nEarth has been made stable with the help of mountains:\nوَأَلْقَىٰ فِي الْأَرْضِ رَوَاسِيَ أَن تَمِيدَ بِكُمْ\nAnd He has cast into the earth firmly set mountains, lest it shift with you.\n[An-Nahl: 15]\nوَجَعَلْنَا فِي الْأَرْضِ رَوَاسِيَ أَن تَمِيدَ بِهِمْ وَجَعَلْنَا فِيهَا فِجَاجًا سُبُلًا لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُونَ\nAnd We placed within the earth firmly set mountains, lest it should shift with them, and We made therein [mountain] passes [as] roads that they might be guided.\n[Al-Anbiya: 31]\nخَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ بِغَيْرِ عَمَدٍ تَرَوْنَهَا ۖ وَأَلْقَىٰ فِي الْأَرْضِ رَوَاسِيَ أَن تَمِيدَ بِكُمْ وَبَثَّ فِيهَا مِن كُلِّ دَابَّةٍ ۚ\nHe created the heavens without pillars that you see and has cast into the earth firmly set mountains, lest it should shift with you, and dispersed therein from every creature.\n[Luqman: 10]\nThe mountains keep the movement and pace of the earth stable.\nAllah(swt) has created everything in perfect balance:\n﴿إِنَّا كُلَّ شَيْءٍ خَلَقْنَاهُ بِقَدَرٍ ٤٩ وَمَا أَمْرُنَا إِلَّا وَاحِدَةٌ كَلَمْحٍ بِالْبَصَرِ ٥٠﴾\nIndeed, all things We created with predestination. And Our command is but one, like the blinking of the eye.\n[Al-Qamar: 49, 50]\nThat is, just as it takes a split second to blink an eye, within no time the command of Allah(swt) gets implemented. And whatever happens is according to a design so that the balance of this world is maintained.\nA day with Allah(swt) is equivalent to a thousand years according to our perception:\nيُدَبِّرُ الْأَمْرَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ ثُمَّ يَعْرُجُ إِلَيْهِ فِي يَوْمٍ كَانَ مِقْدَارُهُ أَلْفَ سَنَةٍ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّونَ\nHe arranges [each] matter from the heaven to the earth; then it will ascend to Him in a Day, the extent of which is a thousand years of those which you count.\n[As-Sajda: 5]\nThat is, Allah(swt) arranges the matters like birth and death, health and sickness, war and peace of all creatures from His Throne, where ‘Lauhe-Mahfoos’ is also present. Details about one thousand years are a matter of one day with Him. From this we come to know about His sole Sovereignty.\nThe skies have been decorated with the help of the stars:\nإِنَّا زَيَّنَّا السَّمَاءَ الدُّنْيَا بِزِينَةٍ الْكَوَاكِبِ\nIndeed, We have adorned the nearest heaven with an adornment of stars.\n[As-Saffat: 6]\nوَلَقَدْ زَيَّنَّا السَّمَاءَ الدُّنْيَا بِمَصَابِيحَ وَجَعَلْنَاهَا رُجُومًا لِّلشَّيَاطِينِ ۖ\nAnd We have certainly beautified the nearest heaven with stars and have made [from] them what is thrown at the devils.\n[Al-Mulk: 5]\nLife forms are found on the other skies as well:\nوَلِلَّهِ يَسْجُدُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ مِن دَابَّةٍ وَالْمَلَائِكَةُ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ\nAnd to Allah prostrates whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth of creatures, and the angels [as well], and they are not arrogant.\n[An-Nahl: 49]\nFor the people of the earth, the rising and setting of the moon is for determining the time:\nيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْأَهِلَّةِ ۖ قُلْ هِيَ مَوَاقِيتُ لِلنَّاسِ وَالْحَجِّ ۗ\nThey ask you, [O Muhammad], about the new moons. Say, \"They are measurements of time for the people and for Hajj.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 189]\nهُوَ الَّذِي جَعَلَ الشَّمْسَ ضِيَاءً وَالْقَمَرَ نُورًا وَقَدَّرَهُ مَنَازِلَ لِتَعْلَمُوا عَدَدَ السِّنِينَ وَالْحِسَابَ ۚ\nIt is He who made the sun a shining light and the moon a derived light and determined for it phases - that you may know the number of years and account [of time].\n[Yunus: 5]\nSun is a shining light means that it has light of its own. Moon is a derived light means that it does not have light of its own but reflects the light of the sun.\nAt another place the Holy Quran says:\nتَبَارَكَ الَّذِي جَعَلَ فِي السَّمَاءِ بُرُوجًا وَجَعَلَ فِيهَا سِرَاجًا وَقَمَرًا مُّنِيرًا\nBlessed is He who has placed in the sky great stars and placed therein a [burning] lamp and luminous moon.\n[Al-Furqan: 61]\nHere by ‘Buruj’ are meant the stars which have an area of their own and they do not overlap each other. Earth has been created in such a way that creatures can live on it and plants can grow in its soil.\n﴿وَالْأَرْضَ مَدَدْنَاهَا وَأَلْقَيْنَا فِيهَا رَوَاسِيَ وَأَنبَتْنَا فِيهَا مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مَّوْزُونٍ ١٩ وَجَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ فِيهَا مَعَايِشَ وَمَن لَّسْتُمْ لَهُ بِرَازِقِينَ ٢٠﴾\nAnd the earth - We have spread it and cast therein firmly set mountains and caused to grow therein [something] of every well-balanced thing. And We have made for you therein means of living and [for] those for whom you are not providers.\n[Al-Hijr: 19, 20]\nStars are useful in guiding the people travelling on land and on the seas:\nوَهُوَ الَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ النُّجُومَ لِتَهْتَدُوا بِهَا فِي ظُلُمَاتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ ۗ قَدْ فَصَّلْنَا الْآيَاتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَعْلَمُونَ\nAnd it is He who placed for you the stars that you may be guided by them through the darknesses of the land and sea. We have detailed the signs for a people who know.\n[Al-An’am: 97]\nوَبِالنَّجْمِ هُمْ يَهْتَدُونَ\nAnd by the stars they are [also] guided.\n[An-Nahl: 16]\nEarth has been made habitable:\n﴿وَالْأَرْضَ مَدَدْنَاهَا وَأَلْقَيْنَا فِيهَا رَوَاسِيَ وَأَنبَتْنَا فِيهَا مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مَّوْزُونٍ ١٩ وَجَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ فِيهَا مَعَايِشَ وَمَن لَّسْتُمْ لَهُ بِرَازِقِينَ ٢٠﴾\nAnd the earth - We have spread it and cast therein firmly set mountains and caused to grow therein [something] of every well-balanced thing. And We have made for you therein means of living and [for] those for whom you are not providers.\n[Al-Hijr: 19, 20]\n﴿وَأَنزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً بِقَدَرٍ فَأَسْكَنَّاهُ فِي الْأَرْضِ ۖ وَإِنَّا عَلَىٰ ذَهَابٍ بِهِ لَقَادِرُونَ ١٨ فَأَنشَأْنَا لَكُم بِهِ جَنَّاتٍ مِّن نَّخِيلٍ وَأَعْنَابٍ لَّكُمْ فِيهَا فَوَاكِهُ كَثِيرَةٌ وَمِنْهَا تَأْكُلُونَ ١٩﴾\nAnd We have sent down rain from the sky in a measured amount and settled it in the earth. And indeed, We are Able to take it away. And We brought forth for you thereby gardens of palm trees and grapevines in which for you are abundant fruits and from which you eat.\n[Al-Mu’minun: 18, 19]\nThat is, this earth has been a means of livelihood for humans and other creatures. Whatever we know till now about the resources of the earth accounts for about 4 percent of the total resources. 96 percent are still unknown. This proves the fact that Allah(swt) has made everything in a definite measure.\nThis universe is full of stars around which the planets are revolving in their fixed orbits. Due to gravitational forces they do not get out of their orbits. In the same way the sun is also revolving around some celestial body. Scientists have not been able to determine the exact number of these stars and celestial bodies.\nوَالسَّمَاءَ بَنَيْنَاهَا بِأَيْدٍ وَإِنَّا لَمُوسِعُونَ\nAnd the heaven We constructed with strength, and indeed, We are [its] expander.\n[Adh-Dhariyat: 47]\nEverything in this universe is moving in its own path:\n﴿وَالشَّمْسُ تَجْرِي لِمُسْتَقَرٍّ لَّهَا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ تَقْدِيرُ الْعَزِيزِ الْعَلِيمِ ٣٨ وَالْقَمَرَ قَدَّرْنَاهُ مَنَازِلَ حَتَّىٰ عَادَ كَالْعُرْجُونِ الْقَدِيمِ ٣٩ لَا الشَّمْسُ يَنبَغِي لَهَا أَن تُدْرِكَ الْقَمَرَ وَلَا اللَّيْلُ سَابِقُ النَّهَارِ ۚ وَكُلٌّ فِي فَلَكٍ يَسْبَحُونَ ٤٠﴾\nAnd the sun runs [on course] toward its stopping point. That is the determination of the Exalted in Might, the Knowing. And the moon - We have determined for it phases, until it returns [appearing] like the old date stalk. It is not allowable for the sun to reach the moon, nor does the night overtake the day, but each, in an orbit, is swimming.\n[Ya-sin: 38-40]\nOrbits are the fixed routes along which all the celestial bodies keep moving. The moon revolves round the earth, the earth revolves round the sun and the sun is revolving round some other celestial body. No planet or star clashes with each other and the day this happens will be the Last Day. On that day everything will perish except the name of Allah(swt).\nوَيَبْقَىٰ وَجْهُ رَبِّكَ ذُو الْجَلَالِ وَالْإِكْرَامِ\nAnd there will remain the Face of your Lord, Owner of Majesty and Honor.\n[Ar-Rahman: 27]"],[92,"§Ehsaan\nThe word ‘Ehsaan’ is used again and again in the Holy Quran which means ‘act of kindness’ or ‘virtuous deed’. Ehsaan can be done for others or for oneself.\nIn the first instance, ‘Ehsaan’ can be done without expecting anything in return. For example:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ وَالْإِحْسَانِ وَإِيتَاءِ ذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَيَنْهَىٰ عَنِ الْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ وَالْبَغْيِ ۚ\nIndeed, Allah orders justice and good conduct and giving to relatives and forbids immorality and bad conduct and oppression. [An-Nahl: 90]\nSometimes Ehsaan is in return for some Ehsaan. For example:\nهَلْ جَزَاءُ الْإِحْسَانِ إِلَّا الْإِحْسَانُ\nIs there any Reward for Good - other than Good?\n[Ar-Rahman: 60]\nEhsaan can be for oneself also as is narrated in one Sahih Hadith. The Holy Prophet said:\n“Ehsaan is that you worship Allah(swt) thinking that you are seeing Him(swt). And if you cannot do so then think that He(swt) is seeing you.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 50 and Sahih Muslim, 8)\nThis means that when we worship Almighty Allah(swt), we should perceive Him or at least know that He(swt) is watching our every action and it is being recorded in our ‘Book of Deeds’ which will be presented to us on the Day of Judgement and we have to account for each and everything. If a person lives this life in this state of ‘Ehsaan’, then there is no possibility of his doing wrong deeds. In fact, the prevalence of sins everywhere today is because we have let go of this concept of Ehsaan."],[93,"§Elephant\nThe elephant has been described at only one place in the Holy Quran:\nأَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصْحَابِ الْفِيلِ\nHave you not considered, [O Muhammad], how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant?\n[Al-Feel: 1]\nWho were these ‘companions of the elephant’? For detailed information see ‘As-Sahabul Feel.’"],[94,"§Envy\nEnvy is a shameful disease which afflicts the hearts on seeing the favors bestowed by Allah(swt) on somebody. The first creature to feel jealousy was Iblees whose heart was filled with it when he saw the importance being given to Adam(as). So, blinded by envy, he refused to prostrate before him and became the first creature to disobey Allah(swt).\nAllah(swt) granted many favors to the Holy Prophet(saws) as a result of which the Jews, Christians and disbelievers became envious of him. This jealousy made a chieftain ‘Waleed-bin-Mugheera’ comment “So, Muhammad(saws) is receiving revelations? Were none of the chieftains of Makka and Taif worthy of receiving revelations?” Referring to this the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَقَالُوا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنُ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٍ مِّنَ الْقَرْيَتَيْنِ عَظِيمٍ ٣١ أَهُمْ يَقْسِمُونَ رَحْمَتَ رَبِّكَ ۚ نَحْنُ قَسَمْنَا بَيْنَهُم مَّعِيشَتَهُمْ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا ۚ وَرَفَعْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ فَوْقَ بَعْضٍ دَرَجَاتٍ لِّيَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُهُم بَعْضًا سُخْرِيًّا ۗ وَرَحْمَتُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّا يَجْمَعُونَ ٣٢﴾\nAlso, they say: \"Why is not this Qur'an sent down to some leading man in either of the two (chief) cities?\" Is it they who would portion out the Mercy of thy Lord? It is We Who portion out between them their livelihood in the life of this world: and We raise some of them above others in ranks, so that some may command work from others. But the Mercy of thy Lord is better than the (wealth) which they amass.\n[Az-Zukhruf: 31-32]\nHere the word ‘Rahmat’ is used which means ‘mercy’ and this was a quality bestowed on the Holy Prophet(saws). It was due to this envy that the ‘people of the book’ tried to detract him from his faith:\nوَدَّ كَثِيرٌ مِّنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ لَوْ يَرُدُّونَكُم مِّن بَعْدِ إِيمَانِكُمْ كُفَّارًا حَسَدًا مِّنْ عِندِ أَنفُسِهِم مِّن بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْحَقُّ ۖ فَاعْفُوا وَاصْفَحُوا حَتَّىٰ يَأْتِيَ اللَّهُ بِأَمْرِهِ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ\nQuite a number of the People of the Book wish they could turn you (people) back to infidelity after ye have believed, from selfish envy, after the Truth hath become Manifest unto them: But forgive and overlook, Till Allah accomplish His purpose; for Allah hath power over all things.\n[Al-Baqara: 109]\nSo, Allah(swt) had given the Holy Prophet(saws) advance warning that these people would be jealous of him:\n﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ ١ مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ ٢ وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ ٣ وَمِن شَرِّ النَّفَّاثَاتِ فِي الْعُقَدِ ٤ وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ ٥﴾\nSay: I seek refuge with the Lord of the Dawn. From the mischief of created things; From the mischief of Darkness as it overspreads; And from the mischief of the envious one as he practises envy.\n[Al-Falaq: 1-5]\nEven the Sahih Hadith warn us to guard against envy as it is an affliction of the heart:\n“Do not hate, envy or plot against each other but live together as brothers.”\nAccording to another Sahih Hadith:\n“Faith and envy cannot co-exist in a momin’s heart.” (Sahih Ibn-Hibbaan, 4587)\nEnvy means that we wish some favor bestowed by Allah(swt) on someone to be taken away. This is against the concept of belief in Allah(swt), because He(swt) is the only One who either grants favors or takes them away. So, this sort of wishing can only be done by someone who has not completely believed in Allah(swt) in the true sense.\nOne other quality which is similar to ‘envy’ is something called ‘Gibta’ in Arabic. It means ‘yearn’ or ‘wish’ or ‘aspire’ for something. It does not mean that we wish for someone’s favors to end but that we also wish for something similar. This is actually a good quality and we need to cultivate it. For example when we see a learned person, we also wish that we were equally learned. We should especially have this quality in the matter of competing with each other in doing good deeds.\nوَفِي ذَٰلِكَ فَلْيَتَنَافَسِ الْمُتَنَافِسُونَ\nAnd for this let those aspire, who have aspirations.\n[Al-Mutaffifin: 26]\nAccording to a Sahih Hadith:\n“In two things, envy is permissible. One when somebody has been given lots of wealth and he spends it in the right way and second when somebody has been given knowledge and wisdom and he uses it to dispense justice and also teaches it to others.” (Sahih Bukhari, 73 and Sahih Muslim, 816)\nHere even though the word ‘envy’ is used, the sense in which it is used means ‘wish’ or ‘aspire’ because it is not being wished that the favor should end."],[95,"§Etekaf\nEtekaf is a form of worship which is done in solitude. The method is that a person cuts himself off from his normal worldly life for a few days and spends all his time in the remembrance of Almighty Allah(swt) so that he can purify his soul. This is mainly done during the last ten days of the month of Ramadan as can be seen from the life of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nThe Holy Quran says in this connection:\nوَلَا تُبَاشِرُوهُنَّ وَأَنتُمْ عَاكِفُونَ فِي الْمَسَاجِدِ ۗ\nBut do not associate with your wives while ye are in retreat in the mosques.\n[Al-Baqara: 187]\nBased on the above verse and the teachings of the Holy Prophet(saws), the knowledge which we have gained about Etekaf is as follows:\nWhile in Etekaf, there should be no association with one’s wife.\nEtekaf should be observed in a mosque, that too in a Jamaa masjid so that it is not necessary to go out for the Friday prayers.\nEven ladies can observe Etekaf as the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) did. But only if arrangements can be made for their security and food and water. If not, then the women should not observe Etekaf.\nThere is no evidence of Etekaf being observed at home.\nIf Etekaf is observed during the month of Ramadan, then it is compulsory to fast and if it is observed in the other months, then fasting is not obligatory.\nIf for some reason the person observing Etekaf comes out of it, then it is not necessary to do it again. But if it is as a result of some vow, then it has to be observed again.\nThe person observing Etekaf should not come out of the mosque except for some special needs.\nThe person observing Etekaf should spend all his time in offering salah, reciting the Holy Quran and in the remembrance of Allah(swt) and desist from useless talk with others.\nIf on coming out of the mosque for some special need, the person meets somebody then, he should offer salam, enquire as to his well-being and continue on his way.\nIt is better to observe Etekaf in a Jamaa masjid where there are toilet and drinking water facilities. If not, it is allowed to go home or to the forest for these needs.\nEtekaf is not obligatory upon anybody but every mosque should make arrangements for it. The largest number of people observe Etekaf in ‘Baitullah’ in Makka. According to a statement issued by the committee of Baitullah, in the year 2005, fifty thousand people observed Etekaf in Baitullah and of these approximately twenty thousand were women.\nIf any woman has her period during her Etekaf, then she should discontinue her Etekaf, come out of the mosque and return home."],[96,"§Fasting\nFasting is called ‘saum’ in Arabic which means ‘to stop.’ That is, a fasting person stops himself from eating, drinking and intercourse from dawn to dusk. Fasting is an excellent form of controlling one’s senses.\nEating in excess only further increases our desires. And Satan who moves with the blood in our veins can easily lead us astray. So, fasting is a way to control our desires.\nEven before Islam, fasting had been prescribed. But some people made it the sole aim of their life and adopted monasticism and asceticism. Islam is a moderate religion so while it prescribes fasting, it does not make it the sole aim of life. Hence it is forbidden to fast on all days. Fasting is advised on various occasions but only fasting during the month of Ramadan has been made obligatory :\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ\nO you who have believed, decreed upon you is fasting as it was decreed upon those before you that you may become righteous.\n[Al-Baqara: 183]\nFasting mentioned in the above verse is fasting in the month of Ramadan because it is the sacred month during which the Holy Quran was revealed. Hence Ramadan has been made the month of fasting, an excellent form of worship:\nشَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِي أُنزِلَ فِيهِ الْقُرْآنُ هُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ وَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِّنَ الْهُدَىٰ وَالْفُرْقَانِ ۚ فَمَن شَهِدَ مِنكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ ۖ وَمَن كَانَ مَرِيضًا أَوْ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِّنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ ۗ يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ بِكُمُ الْيُسْرَ وَلَا يُرِيدُ بِكُمُ الْعُسْرَ وَلِتُكْمِلُوا الْعِدَّةَ وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ مَا هَدَاكُمْ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ\nThe month of Ramadhan [is that] in which was revealed the Qur'an, a guidance for the people and clear proofs of guidance and criterion. So whoever sights [the new moon of] the month, let him fast it; and whoever is ill or on a journey - then an equal number of other days. Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship and [wants] for you to complete the period and to glorify Allah for that [to] which He has guided you; and perhaps you will be grateful.\n[Al-Baqara: 185]\nWhat is fasting? Abstaining from food and drink and intercourse from dawn till dusk seeking the pleasure of Allah(swt) is fasting. Fasting helps in purifying one’s senses and in controlling oneself. That is why the people who cannot control their senses in spite of remaining hungry and thirsty from dawn till dusk are being criticized.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Somebody who has not quit telling lies and practicing them, Allah(swt) does not need his going hungry and thirsty.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1903)\nIn another sahih hadith, stressing the importance of fasting, the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“'All acts of worship a man does, belong to him, except fasting which is for Me, and I will reward it.' Fasting is a shield. When anyone of you is fasting, he should not engage in sexual activities nor raise his voice; or if anyone reviles him or quarrels with him, he should say: 'I am fasting.' By Him, in Whose Hand is the life of Muhammad, the breath of a fasting person is sweeter to Allah(swt) on the Day of Resurrection than the fragrance of musk. The one who fasts has two occasions of joy, one when he breaks the fast, he is glad with the breaking of fast, and one when he meets his Rubb, he is glad with his fast.“\n(Sahih Bukhari 1904 and Sahih Muslim 1151)\nIt is forbidden not to fast during the month of Ramadan without a valid reason. There is a hadith which says that if a person does not fast during the month of Ramadan without a valid reason, it will not be compensated even if he fasts his entire life. This hadith is found in the books of sunan like Abu Dawood 2396, Tirmizi 723, Ibn-Maaja 1672 etc., but the scholars of hadith are of the opinion that it is ‘Zaeef’.\nIf while fasting a person breaks it by eating or drinking or having intercourse, then he should free a slave as compensation. If not, then he should fast for two months. If he cannot do it, then he should feed sixty poor people. (See Bukhari 1936 and Sahih Muslim 1111)\nThis is when the husband has had intercourse without the consent of the wife. If it is with the consent of both the husband and wife, then the compensation or ‘kaffara’ applies to both. But it is allowed in the night after breaking the fast.\nBelow are described a few fasts which are not obligatory:\n1. Fasting for six days during the month of ‘Shawwal’ after Ramadan: It is narrated in one sahih hadith that a person who fasts the whole month of Ramadan and then fasts for the six days of Shawwal is like the one who has fasted his whole life. (See Sahih Muslim 1164)\n2. Fasting on the day of Arafat: That is, fasting on the day when the hajis assemble in the grounds of Arafat for the worship of Allah(swt). This is 9 Zilhijja according to Makka. The sins of the preceding one year and the succeeding year of the person who fasts on this day will be forgiven. (See Sahih Muslim 1162)\nBut it is better for the hajis that they do not observe this fast.\n3. The fast of Ashura: That is, fasting on the tenth day of Muharram. This was previously obligatory but when the fasts during Ramadan were made obligatory, this was made ‘nafl’ or optional.\n4. Fasting on the 13th, 14th and 15th days of every month of the Islamic calendar: It is narrated in the sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) always fasted on these days.\n5. Fasts during the month of Shaban: Other than the month of Ramadan, the month in which the Holy Prophet(saws) fasted most was the month of Shaban. (See Bukhari, 1969 and Muslim, 1156)\n6. Fasting on Mondays and Thursdays: The Holy Prophet(saws) would invariably fast on these days because on these days an account of the deeds of men is sent to Allah(swt). It is narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Because I was born on a Monday and on the same day the Holy Quran was revealed to me, I fast on this day.” (See Sahih Muslim, 1162)\n7. Fast of Dawood: Fasting on alternate days is called ‘Saum-e-Dawood’.\n(See Sahih Bukhari 1153 and Muslim, 1159)\nThe above are a few fasts which though not obligatory have great rewards. These are for both men and women. But in the case of optional or ‘nafl’ fasts, a woman has to take the permission of her husband. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“It is not permissible for a woman to observe the optional or nafl fast without the permission of the husband while he is at home.”\n(See Sahih Bukhari 5192 and Muslim 1026)\nBelow are described a few fasts which are ‘makrooh’ or disliked by Allah(swt):\n1. Fasting one’s whole life: Fasting throughout one’s life is makrooh or ‘not liked.’ It is narrated in one sahih hadith that a person who fasts his entire life is like the one who has not fasted at all. (Sahih Bukhari, 1979 and Muslim, 1159)\n2. Fasting only on Fridays: Jabir questioned the Holy Prophet(saws) if it is forbidden to fast on Fridays and the Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “Yes.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1984 and Muslim, 1143)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that we should not fast only on Fridays. It should be combined with the preceding day or the succeeding day. (Sahih Bukhari, 1986 and Muslim, 1144)\nFasting on Fridays is not liked because it is a festival day and we should not fast on such a day. But in case we fast on the day before that also or the day after that also, it is permissible.\n3. Fasting one or two days before the start of Ramadan: The Holy Prophet(saws) has forbidden fasting one or two days before the month of Ramadan. (Sahih Bukhari, 1914 and Muslim, 1082)\n4. Fasting on Idain (that is Id-ul-Fitr and Id-ul-Azha): The Holy Prophet(saws) has forbidden fasting on these two days.(Sahih Bukhari, 1197 and Muslim, 827)\n5. Fasting on the days of Tashreeq: Zilhajja 11,12 and 13 are called the days of Tashreeq. Sacrifice is done on these days. That is why the Holy Prophet(saws) has said:\n“These are the days for eating and drinking and remembering Allah(swt). That is, they are not for fasting.”\n(Sahih Muslim 1042)\nSad-bin-Abi Waqqas narrates that the Holy Prophet(saws) ordered him to make this announcement in Mina:\n“These are the days for eating and drinking. Fasting is not for these days.”\n(Musnad Ahmad, 1:169)\nOnly a haji who is unable to sacrifice an animal when it is obligatory upon him can fast on these days as is mentioned in the Holy Quran:\nفَإِذَا أَمِنتُمْ فَمَن تَمَتَّعَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الْحَجِّ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْيِ ۚ فَمَن لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ ثَلَاثَةِ أَيَّامٍ فِي الْحَجِّ وَسَبْعَةٍ إِذَا رَجَعْتُمْ ۗ تِلْكَ عَشَرَةٌ كَامِلَةٌ ۗ\nAnd when you are secure, then whoever performs 'umrah [during the Hajj months] followed by Hajj [offers] what can be obtained with ease of sacrificial animals. And whoever cannot find [or afford such an animal] - then a fast of three days during Hajj and of seven when you have returned [home]. Those are ten complete [days].\n[Al-Baqara: 196]\nThat is, if he could not fast for three days before Haj, then he can do so in the days of Tashreeq. (See Sahih Bukhari, 1999). This is the opinion of Ibn-Umar and Aisha(ra) and also of the other scholars. There is no hadith regarding this in connection with the Holy Prophet(saws)."],[97,"§Fateh-Mubeen\n‘Fateh-Mubeen’ means a clear victory. The treaty with the disbelievers of Makka which took place at ‘Hudaibiya’ in 6 A.H. has been described as ‘Fateh-Mubeen’ by Allah(swt). The description is as follows. The Holy Prophet(saws) had a dream that he(saws) was entering Makka and shaving his head. He(saws) was very happy that he(saws) will get a chance to perform Umra. The same year, in the month of Ziqada he(saws) started towards Makka along with fifteen hundred companions. They took their sacrificial animals also along with them. He camped at a place called ‘Hadaibiya’, twenty two kilometers from Makka. When the people of Makka heard about it, they got ready for war. The Holy Prophet(saws) sent three of his representatives one after the other with the message that they had not come to fight but to circumambulate the Holy Kaaba and perform Umra. When ‘Usman bin Affan’ was sent, he got slightly delayed. Meanwhile the rumour started spreading that he had been killed. The Holy Prophet(saws) assembled his companions under a tree named ‘Samura’ and took a pledge to do jihad. This pledge or baith is called ‘Baith-e-Rizwan.’ When the people of Makka came to know of this, they let go ‘Usman’ and sent ‘Suhail-bin-Umr’ along with him for conducting talks. A few details of these talks were:\n1. None of the two sides will attack the other for ten years.\n2. If some Muslim goes from Makka to Madina, then he will be returned. But if someone goes from Madina to Makka, he will not be returned.\n3. The tribes of Arab can sign a pact with anybody.\n4. The Muslims should go back this year without performing Umra and return the next year for performing Umra.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) stayed there for twenty days and then went back. The Muslims were unhappy with this treaty because they felt that the Muslims were the losers. The Holy Prophet(saws) was still on his way to Madina when the surah-48, Al-Fath was revealed in which this treaty was described as a clear victory. This made the Muslims very happy and due to this treaty, the Muslims triumphed over Makka and Islam entered every house of Arabia."],[98,"§Fatwa\n‘Fatwa’ is an Arabic word which means to ask or express the religious opinion. For example when the king of Egypt asked his chiefs the meaning of his dream. When he came to know that his prisoner Yusuf(as) would be able to tell him the meaning of his dream, the king summoned Yusuf(as) to him.\nFor a detailed description about this incident see Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verses-43-49.\nIn the same way, when the people asked the Holy Prophet(saws) about orphan women, the answer was given in surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-127.\nAnd when people questioned about ‘kalala’(those who did not have any offspring), Allah(swt) answered it in surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-176.\nIf some religious matter needs to be clarified, the question should be put to a religious scholar as commanded by the Holy Quran. (See Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-43)\nSuch a religious scholar who can give opinion regarding religious issues is called a ‘mufti’. The mufti should not give a fatwa which goes against the teachings of the Holy Quran or the narrations of the sahih hadith. Any fatwa which goes against the Holy Quran or the sahih hadith shall not be accepted. So, the mufti should be well-versed in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith lest he gives a wrong fatwa. In many countries, the Islamic institutions or the rulers in the case of Muslim countries have formed a ‘Dar-ul-Fatwa’ which has a ‘head mufti’. He has a consulting committee. When some question is raised this committee answers the question due to which the possibility of mistakes is greatly reduced.\nIt should be borne in mind that ‘fatwa’ is about new issues about which the mufti has to do ijtihad. Ijtihad (Arabic اجتهاد) is a technical term of Islamic law that describes the process of making a legal decision by independent interpretation of the legal sources, the Qur’an and the Sunnah. This is the reason the same problem may be interpreted in different ways by different muftis. This is one of the specialities of Islam that it gives freedom to the scholars to interpret a problem according to their knowledge and give their fatwa independently. We come to know from this that Islam is comprehensive and thus proves that Islam can be followed at all times and in all places with the greatest ease."],[99,"§Fig\nFig which is called ‘Teen’ in Arabic is a kind of tree which is found mostly in Syria and Palestine. Its height is between 5 and 10 meters and its branches begin spreading out right from the ground itself. It is said that its fruit appears before its leaves. It can be eaten fresh or dried. Hakeems use it in many of their medicines and it is particularly effective in the case of stomach ailments. According to the Holy Bible prophet Isaiah(as) was cured of his boils with the help of figs.\nThen Isaiah said, “Prepare a poultice of figs.” They did so and applied it to the boil, and he recovered.\n(Holy Bible, 2 Kings 20:7)\nIt is due to the various benefits of fig that Allah(swt) swears by it and says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَالتِّينِ وَالزَّيْتُونِ ١ وَطُورِ سِينِينَ ٢ وَهَٰذَا الْبَلَدِ الْأَمِينِ ٣ لَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْإِنسَانَ فِي أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍ ٤﴾\nBy the fig and the olive . And [by] Mount Sinai .And [by] this secure city [Makkah], We have certainly created man in the best of stature;\n[At-Teen: 1-4]"],[100,"§Pharaoh(Firaun)\nThe literal meaning of Pharaoh(Firaun) is ‘son of sun’. As the people of Egypt worshipped the sun, they gave the title of ‘Pharaoh(Firaun)’ to their king. They considered their king to be the incarnation of their sun-god and hence worshipped him. So, we come to know that ‘Pharaoh(Firaun)’ wasn’t the name of a particular king but was the title given to all their kings. Just as the Roman kings were called ‘Khaiser’, kings of Iran were called ‘kisra’, the Turkish kings were called ‘Kha’khans, the Egyptian kings were called Pharaohs(Firaun). Five Pharaohs(Firaun) have been described by name in the Bible. They belonged to the period after Musa(as). These were :\n1. Shishak 2. So 3. Necho 4. Hophra and 5. Taharqa\nTheir brief description is as follows:\n1. Shishak: He was the king of Egypt during the time of Sulaiman(as). When Sulaiman(as) wanted to kill Jeroboam, he ran away to Shishak and remained there till his death. (See 1 Kings 11:40)\nAfter Jeroboam became king, this same Shishak attacked the land of Israel and took away whatever was there in the kingdom of Sulaiman(as). (See 1 Kings, 14:25)\n2. So: Hoshea, the king of Israel sought the help of So, the king of Egypt against Shalmaneser king of Assyria. But So could not help him and therefore Shalmaneser won and the kingdom of Israel was in his hands for three years.(See: 2 Kings, 17:3-4)\n3. Taharqa: He was the king of Cush. He became the king of Egypt around 688 B.C. (See 2 Kings, 19:9 and Isaiah, 37:9)\n4. Necho: He reigned over Egypt from 609 to 583 B.C. He was the first king who tried to connect the Red sea and the White sea. After lakhs of people were killed, he changed his mind. After two and a half thousand years, the Egyptians dug a canal and named it the Suez canal.\nFor detailed information about the Pharaoh(Firaun) Necho, see 2 Kings, 23:29.\n5. Hophra: He was the successor of Necho.\nThese are the five Pharaohs(Firaun) who are mentioned in the Bible. Some Pharaohs(Firaun) have been described in the Bible but their names haven’t been mentioned. They are the Pharaohs(Firaun) during the times of Ibraheem(as), Yusuf(as) and Musa(as). That is why there is a difference of opinion among the historians concerning their names. In the Holy Quran, the description about the Pharaoh(Firaun) during the time of Musa(as) occurs seventy-four times. Scholars are of the opinion that the king in whose palace Musa(as) was brought up was named ‘Simat’. Some say he was ‘Pathameen’ while some say he was Ramesses II who was the king from 1527 to 1407 B.C. The Pharaoh(Firaun) to whom Musa(as) went with the message of Allah(swt) was Minfatah and it was this same king who chased the Bani-Israel and was drowned in the sea in the end.\nThe Holy Quran is the word of Allah(swt) and is a guidance for the entire mankind and therefore unnecessary details are not mentioned in it. That is why his description is very brief. We have to note how he has been described in the Holy Quran, how he tormented the believers and what his ultimate end was.\nPharaoh(Firaun) killed the sons of Bani-Israel and let the women live:\nوَإِذْ نَجَّيْنَاكُم مِّنْ آلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُومُونَكُمْ سُوءَ الْعَذَابِ يُذَبِّحُونَ أَبْنَاءَكُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيُونَ نِسَاءَكُمْ ۚ وَفِي ذَٰلِكُم بَلَاءٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ عَظِيمٌ\nAnd [recall] when We saved your forefathers from the people of Pharaoh, who afflicted you with the worst torment, slaughtering your [newborn] sons and keeping your females alive. And in that was a great trial from your Lord.\n[Al-Baqara: 49]\nPharaoh(Firaun) and his tribe rejected the clear signs sent by Allah(swt):\nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِن بَعْدِهِم مُّوسَىٰ بِآيَاتِنَا إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَئِهِ فَظَلَمُوا بِهَا ۖ فَانظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِينَ\nThen We sent after them Moses with Our signs to Pharaoh and his establishment, but they were unjust toward them. So see how was the end of the corrupters.\n[Al-A’raf: 103]\nThe Pharaoh(Firaun) assembled the magicians and tried to falsify the signs of Musa(as). But when Musa(as) defeated the magicians and they believed in the message of Musa(as), the Pharaoh(Firaun) started using violence. He threatened the magicians that he would hang all of them. This is described in great detail in the Holy Quran:\n﴿قَالَ إِن كُنتَ جِئْتَ بِآيَةٍ فَأْتِ بِهَا إِن كُنتَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ ١٠٦ فَأَلْقَىٰ عَصَاهُ فَإِذَا هِيَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِينٌ ١٠٧ وَنَزَعَ يَدَهُ فَإِذَا هِيَ بَيْضَاءُ لِلنَّاظِرِينَ ١٠٨ قَالَ الْمَلَأُ مِن قَوْمِ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَسَاحِرٌ عَلِيمٌ ١٠٩ يُرِيدُ أَن يُخْرِجَكُم مِّنْ أَرْضِكُمْ ۖ فَمَاذَا تَأْمُرُونَ ١١٠ قَالُوا أَرْجِهْ وَأَخَاهُ وَأَرْسِلْ فِي الْمَدَائِنِ حَاشِرِينَ ١١١ يَأْتُوكَ بِكُلِّ سَاحِرٍ عَلِيمٍ ١١٢ وَجَاءَ السَّحَرَةُ فِرْعَوْنَ قَالُوا إِنَّ لَنَا لَأَجْرًا إِن كُنَّا نَحْنُ الْغَالِبِينَ ١١٣ قَالَ نَعَمْ وَإِنَّكُمْ لَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ ١١٤ قَالُوا يَا مُوسَىٰ إِمَّا أَن تُلْقِيَ وَإِمَّا أَن نَّكُونَ نَحْنُ الْمُلْقِينَ ١١٥ قَالَ أَلْقُوا ۖ فَلَمَّا أَلْقَوْا سَحَرُوا أَعْيُنَ النَّاسِ وَاسْتَرْهَبُوهُمْ وَجَاءُوا بِسِحْرٍ عَظِيمٍ ١١٦ ۞ وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ أَنْ أَلْقِ عَصَاكَ ۖ فَإِذَا هِيَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَأْفِكُونَ ١١٧ فَوَقَعَ الْحَقُّ وَبَطَلَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ١١٨ فَغُلِبُوا هُنَالِكَ وَانقَلَبُوا صَاغِرِينَ ١١٩ وَأُلْقِيَ السَّحَرَةُ سَاجِدِينَ ١٢٠ قَالُوا آمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ١٢١ رَبِّ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ ١٢٢ قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ آمَنتُم بِهِ قَبْلَ أَنْ آذَنَ لَكُمْ ۖ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَمَكْرٌ مَّكَرْتُمُوهُ فِي الْمَدِينَةِ لِتُخْرِجُوا مِنْهَا أَهْلَهَا ۖ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُونَ ١٢٣ لَأُقَطِّعَنَّ أَيْدِيَكُمْ وَأَرْجُلَكُم مِّنْ خِلَافٍ ثُمَّ لَأُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ ١٢٤ قَالُوا إِنَّا إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا مُنقَلِبُونَ ١٢٥ وَمَا تَنقِمُ مِنَّا إِلَّا أَنْ آمَنَّا بِآيَاتِ رَبِّنَا لَمَّا جَاءَتْنَا ۚ رَبَّنَا أَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا وَتَوَفَّنَا مُسْلِمِينَ ١٢٦ وَقَالَ الْمَلَأُ مِن قَوْمِ فِرْعَوْنَ أَتَذَرُ مُوسَىٰ وَقَوْمَهُ لِيُفْسِدُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَيَذَرَكَ وَآلِهَتَكَ ۚ قَالَ سَنُقَتِّلُ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ وَنَسْتَحْيِي نِسَاءَهُمْ وَإِنَّا فَوْقَهُمْ قَاهِرُونَ ١٢٧﴾\n[Pharaoh] said, \"If you have come with a sign, then bring it forth, if you should be of the truthful.\" So Moses threw his staff, and suddenly it was a serpent, manifest. And he drew out his hand; thereupon it was white [with radiance] for the observers. Said the eminent among the people of Pharaoh, \"Indeed, this is a learned magician. Who wants to expel you from your land [through magic], so what do you instruct?\" They said, \"Postpone [the matter of] him and his brother and send among the cities gatherers . Who will bring you every learned magician.\" And the magicians came to Pharaoh. They said, \"Indeed for us is a reward if we are the predominant.\" He said, \"Yes, and, [moreover], you will be among those made near [to me].\" They said, \"O Moses, either you throw [your staff], or we will be the ones to throw [first].\" He said, \"Throw,\" and when they threw, they bewitched the eyes of the people and struck terror into them, and they presented a great [feat of] magic. And We inspired to Moses, \"Throw your staff,\" and at once it devoured what they were falsifying. So the truth was established, and abolished was what they were doing. And Pharaoh and his people were overcome right there and became debased. And the magicians fell down in prostration [to Allah].They said, \"We have believed in the Lord of the worlds, The Lord of Moses and Aaron.\" Said Pharaoh, \"You believed in him before I gave you permission. Indeed, this is a conspiracy which you conspired in the city to expel therefrom its people. But you are going to know. I will surely cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides; then I will surely crucify you all.\" They said, \"Indeed, to our Lord we will return. And you do not resent us except because we believed in the signs of our Lord when they came to us. Our Lord, pour upon us patience and let us die as Muslims [in submission to You].\" And the eminent among the people of Pharaoh said, \"Will you leave Moses and his people to cause corruption in the land and abandon you and your gods?\" [Pharaoh] said, \"We will kill their sons and keep their women alive; and indeed, we are subjugators over them.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 106-127]\nPharaoh(Firaun) was very arrogant:\nوَإِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ لَعَالٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَإِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الْمُسْرِفِينَ\nAnd indeed, Pharaoh was haughty within the land, and indeed, he was of the transgressors.\n[Yunus: 83]\nAllah(swt) commanded Musa(as) to go to the Pharaoh(Firaun) because he had become a transgressor. (See Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-24)\nإِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ عَلَا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَجَعَلَ أَهْلَهَا شِيَعًا يَسْتَضْعِفُ طَائِفَةً مِّنْهُمْ يُذَبِّحُ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيِي نِسَاءَهُمْ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِينَ\nIndeed, the Pharaoh exalted himself in the land and made its people into factions, oppressing a sector among them, slaughtering their [newborn] sons and keeping their females alive. Indeed, he was of the corrupters.\n[Al-Qasas: 4]\nPharaoh(Firaun) claimed to be God:\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ مَا عَلِمْتُ لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرِي فَأَوْقِدْ لِي\nAnd Pharaoh said: O eminent ones, I have not known you to have a god other than me.\n[Al-Qasas: 38]\n﴿فَحَشَرَ فَنَادَىٰ ٢٣ فَقَالَ أَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْأَعْلَىٰ ٢٤﴾\nAnd he gathered [his people] and called out. And said, \"I am your most exalted lord.\"\n[An-Nazi’at: 23, 24]\nThe end of Pharaoh(Firaun):\nWhen the Bani-Israel were leaving Egypt, the Pharaoh(Firaun) chased them and surrounded them when they reached the sea. At the command of Allah(swt), Musa(as) hit the water with his staff and the sea parted in the middle:\nفَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ أَنِ اضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ الْبَحْرَ ۖ فَانفَلَقَ فَكَانَ كُلُّ فِرْقٍ كَالطَّوْدِ الْعَظِيمِ\nThen We inspired to Moses, \"Strike with your staff the sea,\" and it parted, and each portion was like a great towering mountain.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 63]\nThe Bani-Israel crossed the sea using the path which was formed in the middle but when the army of Pharaoh(Firaun) followed, the two parts closed in again and the whole army was drowned. Allah(swt) did not let the corpse of Pharaoh(Firaun) drown but caused it to be thrown out so that it became a lesson to others. The people could see the terrible and shameful end of a person who claimed to be god:\nفَالْيَوْمَ نُنَجِّيكَ بِبَدَنِكَ لِتَكُونَ لِمَنْ خَلْفَكَ آيَةً ۚ وَإِنَّ كَثِيرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِ عَنْ آيَاتِنَا لَغَافِلُونَ\nSo today We will save you in body that you may be to those who succeed you a sign. And indeed, many among the people, of Our signs, are heedless.\n[Yunus: 92]\nSome commentators are of the opinion that the reference here is to the body which has been kept in a museum in Cairo. It is generally felt that it is the same Pharaoh(Firaun) whose body has been preserved as a lesson for the future generations. The people who say this are mistaken in two ways:\nFirstly, it cannot be inferred from the Holy Quran that the body would be preserved till the Last Day or even for a thousand years because the main purpose of throwing out the body from the sea was to show it to the people who considered Pharaoh(Firaun) to be their god and prostrated before him. And the purpose of showing the state of their god to the people was achieved.\nSecondly, it was not proved conclusively that the body was of the Pharaoh(Firaun) who had chased the Bani-Israel. The ‘sign’ in the above verse means that it is a sign for the people of his tribe and a lesson to all future tribes that the end of the people who worship others besides Allah(swt) and who torment others will be as shameful as that of Pharaoh(Firaun).\nThe Bible describes the drowning of Pharaoh(Firaun) and his army as follows:\nThen the Lord said to Moses, “Stretch out your hand over the sea so that the waters may flow back over the Egyptians and their chariots and horsemen.” Moses stretched out his hand over the sea, and at daybreak the sea went back to its place. The Egyptians were fleeing toward it, and the Lord swept them into the sea. The water flowed back and covered the chariots and horsemen—the entire army of Pharaoh that had followed the Israelites into the sea. Not one of them survived.\nBut the Israelites went through the sea on dry ground, with a wall of water on their right and on their left. That day the Lord saved Israel from the hands of the Egyptians, and Israel saw the Egyptians lying dead on the shore. And when the Israelites saw the mighty hand of the Lord displayed against the Egyptians, the people feared the Lord and put their trust in him and in Moses his servant.\n(See Exodus, 14:26-31)\nHere it is being said that Israel saw the Egyptians lying dead on the shore. It is possible that the body of Pharaoh(Firaun) was also among them; in fact it must have been, so that a group of Israelites who were still in doubt about the death of Pharaoh(Firaun) could be convinced about it."]])